($kb$lib-mf-audit-compliance-page$kb$, $kb$mf-audit-compliance-page$kb$, $kb$Mediflow Guide: Compliance & Security$kb$, $kb$Audit & Compliance page: the audit trail and AI compliance report$kb$, $kb$Where: sidebar group Compliance > Audit & Compliance. Visible to Super Admin, Agency Admin and Compliance Manager.

What it shows:
- Four tiles: events recorded (all time for your agency), changes and people in the current view, and how long ago the latest event was.
- Audit log, newest first. Each row shows who did it, their role, the action (create, update, delete, read, export, login) and the type of record. The page says entries can't be edited or deleted.
- Opening this log is itself recorded.

AI compliance report:
1. Click Generate Report.
2. Watch the plain-English summary of each agent's licenses, certifications, AHIP and overdue tasks appear.
3. When it finishes, click Download PDF.

For filters, date ranges, before/after details and CSV export, use Admin > Security & HIPAA checklist > Audit Log tab (see that article).

Note: the log records activity on client, agent and commission records and other areas as they happen. It is a record of what people did, not a pass/fail grade.$kb$, ARRAY[$kb$audit$kb$, $kb$audit log$kb$, $kb$audit trail$kb$, $kb$compliance$kb$, $kb$hipaa$kb$, $kb$who viewed$kb$, $kb$activity log$kb$, $kb$compliance report$kb$, $kb$pdf$kb$, $kb$history$kb$]::text[], 'mediflow_guide', true, false),
($kb$lib-mf-esign-consent$kb$, $kb$mf-esign-consent$kb$, $kb$Mediflow Guide: Compliance & Security$kb$, $kb$E-signature for carrier contracting paperwork and consent fields$kb$, $kb$What exists: an in-house e-signature window (labeled Beta) used for carrier contracting paperwork. Mediflow does not have a separate client Scope of Appointment (SOA) form or e-sign flow.

Where: an agent opens it from the onboarding step "Sign carrier paperwork" (sidebar Main > My Onboarding) by clicking Sign now once paperwork is generated. Super Admin, Agency Admin, Compliance Manager and Agent roles can start one.

To sign:
1. Scroll through the document and tick "I have scrolled through and reviewed".
2. Tick all three consent boxes (electronic business, read and understood, paper copy available).
3. Type your full legal name (required). Optionally draw your signature too.
4. Click Sign and complete.

Closing the window before signing stores nothing. When you sign, Mediflow records your IP address and device on its own, plus the wording version you agreed to. Only the signer or an admin can sign; only an admin can void an envelope (a reason is required).

Client texting consent: on a client's record you can enter a texting consent (TCPA) date and its source; a source is required with a date.

SOA: Call scoring can check whether a scope of appointment was confirmed on a call transcript.$kb$, ARRAY[$kb$e-sign$kb$, $kb$esign$kb$, $kb$signature$kb$, $kb$sign$kb$, $kb$consent$kb$, $kb$soa$kb$, $kb$scope of appointment$kb$, $kb$contracting$kb$, $kb$tcpa$kb$, $kb$paperwork$kb$, $kb$electronic signature$kb$]::text[], 'mediflow_guide', true, false),
($kb$lib-mf-call-scoring-recording$kb$, $kb$mf-call-scoring-recording$kb$, $kb$Mediflow Guide: Compliance & Security$kb$, $kb$Call scoring and call recording: what Mediflow does today$kb$, $kb$Where: sidebar group Compliance > Call scoring. Super Admin, Agency Admin and Compliance Manager see all calls and can add and review. Agents see only calls linked to calls they placed, and cannot add or review.

What it does: checks call transcripts against a checklist (Medicare sales call, or a general sales checklist) and flags possible do-not-contact requests. It assists review; it is not legal advice or a certification.

Add a transcript:
1. Click Add transcripts.
2. Paste text or upload a TXT, VTT, SRT or JSON file (1 MB max), pick a checklist, optionally add a client phone number and a reference.
3. Open the result to see each finding with the exact words, who said them and when.

Review:
- A reviewer can override a grade with a required note; the automatic result is kept.
- Calls with a failed critical item or an ungraded one are not shown as passed.
- Possible do-not-contact tab: read the quote, then add the number to the do-not-contact list or mark Not a request with a note. Nothing is added automatically.

Look-back import: up to 50 files plus an optional CSV manifest at once.

Not available: it cannot transcribe audio. Call recording is off by default and the setup guide says nothing in the product can turn it on yet.$kb$, ARRAY[$kb$call scoring$kb$, $kb$call recording$kb$, $kb$recording$kb$, $kb$transcript$kb$, $kb$do not call$kb$, $kb$dnc$kb$, $kb$do-not-contact$kb$, $kb$checklist$kb$, $kb$quality$kb$, $kb$review$kb$, $kb$soa$kb$, $kb$softphone$kb$]::text[], 'mediflow_guide', true, false),
($kb$lib-mf-security-hipaa-checklist$kb$, $kb$mf-security-hipaa-checklist$kb$, $kb$Mediflow Guide: Compliance & Security$kb$, $kb$Security & HIPAA checklist: readiness checks, sessions, access review, PHI masking$kb$, $kb$Where: sidebar group Admin > Security & HIPAA checklist. Super Admin, Agency Admin and Compliance Manager can open it. Some actions are Super Admin / Agency Admin only.

It shows live checks worked out from your settings. It is not a certification.

Tabs:
- Readiness checks: controls passing and needing attention (audit logging active, PHI masking for non-privileged roles, data retention set, breach-notification workflow, storage access policy). Generate PDF makes an evidence pack for your auditor (admins only).
- Audit Log: filter by action, record type, dates and user; click a row to see before and after; Export CSV.
- Sessions: see where people are signed in; revoke one session or force logout (admins).
- Access Review: everyone with a login and their role; deactivate or reactivate (admins).
- Login History: sign-in attempts with IP and failure reason.
- Export Log: every data download.
- Security Config (admins): idle sign-out timeout of 15, 30 or 60 minutes, and data retention per record type.

PHI: Super Admin, Agency Admin and Compliance Manager see full client PHI; other roles see masked values. An Agent sees full details only for clients they service. Opening a full enrollment application is audited.$kb$, ARRAY[$kb$hipaa$kb$, $kb$security$kb$, $kb$phi$kb$, $kb$audit trail$kb$, $kb$session timeout$kb$, $kb$force logout$kb$, $kb$access review$kb$, $kb$login history$kb$, $kb$evidence pack$kb$, $kb$data retention$kb$, $kb$masking$kb$, $kb$baa$kb$]::text[], 'mediflow_guide', true, false),
($kb$lib-mf-licensing-certs-renewals$kb$, $kb$mf-licensing-certs-renewals$kb$, $kb$Mediflow Guide: Compliance & Security$kb$, $kb$Licensing, Certifications and License Renewals: tracking expirations$kb$, $kb$Where (sidebar group Compliance):
- Licensing and Certifications: every role can open them (an Agent sees only their own licenses).
- License Renewals: Super Admin, Agency Admin and Compliance Manager.

Licensing: shows each agent's state licenses and a "Renewals coming up" list for the next 90 days. Tiles count expired and expiring licenses at 30 days, 31-60 and 61-90. Search agents or filter by status. Import from CSV needs agentId, stateCode and licenseType; licenseNumber, issueDate, expiryDate and status are optional. A license counts as active only if its status is active and its expiry date has not passed, so a past-date license reads as expired.

Certifications: pick a plan year. The AHIP tab lists each agent's AHIP status; the Carrier certifications tab is a grid of agents by carrier; below is a list expiring in 90 days. Record AHIP and certifications on the agent's profile.

License Renewals:
1. Filter by type (licenses, certifications), days ahead (30 to 180) or urgency: Critical (30 days or less), Warning (31-60), Notice (61+).
2. Click Snooze to hide an item for 30 days.
3. Click Resolve to hide it for one year.

Neither button changes the actual expiry date; update the license or certification itself on the agent's profile.$kb$, ARRAY[$kb$license$kb$, $kb$licensing$kb$, $kb$certification$kb$, $kb$ahip$kb$, $kb$renewal$kb$, $kb$expiring$kb$, $kb$expired$kb$, $kb$state license$kb$, $kb$carrier certification$kb$, $kb$csv import$kb$, $kb$snooze$kb$, $kb$appointed$kb$]::text[], 'mediflow_guide', true, false),
($kb$lib-mf-marketing-approval-complaints$kb$, $kb$mf-marketing-approval-complaints$kb$, $kb$Mediflow Guide: Compliance & Security$kb$, $kb$Marketing Approval and Complaints: submit, review and track$kb$, $kb$Both are in sidebar group Compliance and visible to Super Admin, Agency Admin and Compliance Manager.

Marketing Approval:
1. Click Submit material and fill in: title, type (flyer, social post, email, mailer, TV, radio, web, business card, presentation, script or other), optional carrier, asset link and description.
2. A reviewer changes the status on the row: Submitted, In review, Approved, Rejected, Changes requested or Retired.
3. The person who submitted a piece cannot approve or reject it; a different reviewer must.
4. Approved material is locked; changing its content means resubmitting it.
Tiles show waiting, approved, expiring in 30 days and expired. Approved pieces show their use window when dates are on file; this page has no field for setting dates. Submissions and status changes are logged.

Complaints:
1. Click Log complaint and fill in: subject, description, severity (Critical, High, Medium, Low), source (CMS CTM, beneficiary, carrier, internal, other), category and optional CMS CTM case number. Do not enter member IDs or PHI.
2. Change status on the row: Open, Investigating, Resolved, Closed.
3. Mediflow sets a due date from severity: 2, 5, 10 or 30 days. These are Mediflow's own targets. Late open items show Overdue.
Filter by status, severity or overdue only.$kb$, ARRAY[$kb$marketing$kb$, $kb$marketing approval$kb$, $kb$complaint$kb$, $kb$complaints$kb$, $kb$ctm$kb$, $kb$flyer$kb$, $kb$approval$kb$, $kb$review$kb$, $kb$overdue$kb$, $kb$severity$kb$, $kb$cms$kb$, $kb$material$kb$]::text[], 'mediflow_guide', true, false),
($kb$lib-mf-clients-leads-pipeline$kb$, $kb$mf-clients-leads-pipeline$kb$, $kb$Mediflow Guide: Sales Tools$kb$, $kb$Clients & Leads: contacts, leads, pipeline stages and deals$kb$, $kb$Where: Main > Clients & Leads (Super Admin, Agency Admin, Compliance Manager, Agent Support). Agents use Main > My Clients instead.

Tabs: Contacts, Leads, Pipeline, Inbox, Sequences, Retention.

Contacts: search, filter by status (Lead, Prospect, Enrolled, Retained, Lost) or plan type, add a contact, or select several to assign an agent, add/remove a tag, set status or export CSV. Click a person to open their record (Timeline, Call summaries, Deals, Tasks, Sequences, Applications). Buttons there: SMS, Email, Log, book an appointment, Create Lead, Edit.

Leads: filter by status (New, Contacted, Qualified, Disqualified, Converted). Change a lead's status from its dropdown. A Qualified lead shows Convert, which marks it Converted and sets the contact to Prospect.

Pipeline: pick a pipeline, then use New Deal (pipeline, contact, title, stage, estimated value). Each deal card has a menu: Move to stage, Mark as won, Mark as lost (optional reason). Tiles show open value, weighted forecast (value x stage chance), won deals and conversion rate. No pipeline yet? Create a pipeline; Mediflow starts it with New Lead, Contacted, Qualified, Application, Enrolled.

My Clients (agents): search the clients assigned to you or whose policy you wrote; open one for details, policies and applications.$kb$, ARRAY[$kb$clients$kb$, $kb$leads$kb$, $kb$contacts$kb$, $kb$crm$kb$, $kb$pipeline$kb$, $kb$deal$kb$, $kb$stage$kb$, $kb$convert lead$kb$, $kb$my clients$kb$, $kb$won$kb$, $kb$lost$kb$, $kb$forecast$kb$, $kb$add contact$kb$]::text[], 'mediflow_guide', true, false),
($kb$lib-mf-lead-routing-live-queue$kb$, $kb$mf-lead-routing-live-queue$kb$, $kb$Mediflow Guide: Sales Tools$kb$, $kb$Inbound lead routing, Live Call Queue and Queue Wallboard$kb$, $kb$Where: Sales Tools > Live Call Queue and Sales Tools > Queue Wallboard (Super Admin and Agency Admin only).

How routing works: when an inbound call or lead arrives from a connected system, Mediflow picks one agent. The agent must be active, licensed in the lead's state, have a current AHIP record, and be certified with that carrier. Among those, the agent with the fewest open leads is picked, and only agents currently marked Available are considered (if no agent has ever checked in, this presence filter is skipped). If nobody qualifies, the call is recorded as missed and a callback is owed. Every decision is logged. Note: the connection to the outside call system (GoHighLevel/Atlas) needs setup on both sides; the code exists but verify it is live before relying on it.

Agents: use the Available/Away toggle at the bottom of the sidebar. Mediflow is set up to drop an agent from the pool if no check-in arrives for about 90 seconds.

Live Call Queue (refreshes every 15 seconds): agents available now, calls routed, missed, coverage gaps (carrier and state combinations with nobody free), routing analytics (24h or 7d), Callbacks owed (with a countdown and a cancel button), agent presence, and the last 50 routing decisions.

Queue Wallboard: a read-only full-screen display for a wall TV with the same live numbers.$kb$, ARRAY[$kb$live call queue$kb$, $kb$wallboard$kb$, $kb$routing$kb$, $kb$inbound$kb$, $kb$lead routing$kb$, $kb$available$kb$, $kb$away$kb$, $kb$presence$kb$, $kb$callback$kb$, $kb$coverage gap$kb$, $kb$missed calls$kb$, $kb$ready to sell$kb$]::text[], 'mediflow_guide', true, false),
($kb$lib-mf-softphone-supervisor$kb$, $kb$mf-softphone-supervisor$kb$, $kb$Mediflow Guide: Sales Tools$kb$, $kb$Softphone and Supervisor dashboard$kb$, $kb$Softphone. Where: Main > Softphone (Super Admin, Agency Admin, Compliance Manager, Agent Support, Agent). Agents only see their own assigned contacts.
1. Type a number on the dial pad, pick a recent call, or search by name. This only finds a contact; you can only call someone on file.
2. Read the OK to call? card: consent on file, not on do-not-call/opt-out list, within calling hours, and agent licensed and certified. Mediflow is set up to treat 8am to 9pm in the contact's time zone as calling hours.
3. Press Call to call from your browser. If calling is not configured it shows Needs setup, and in a demo no real call is placed.
4. After hanging up, choose an outcome and add notes. Choosing do-not-call adds the number to the opt-out list.
You can also log a call made on your own phone. Live transcription, recording, hold/mute/transfer and listen-in are shown as Coming next.

Supervisor. Where: Main > Supervisor (Super Admin, Agency Admin).
Live Floor tab: agents online, available, on a call, routed and missed in 24 hours, open callbacks, coverage gaps; click an agent for details. Refreshes every 15 seconds.
Call Review tab: recent post-call summaries with suggested outcome, risk flags and action items; suggestions are advisory.
Listen-in, whisper, barge and recordings are marked coming soon.$kb$, ARRAY[$kb$softphone$kb$, $kb$dialer$kb$, $kb$call$kb$, $kb$dial pad$kb$, $kb$supervisor$kb$, $kb$ok to call$kb$, $kb$do not call$kb$, $kb$dnc$kb$, $kb$calling hours$kb$, $kb$call review$kb$, $kb$disposition$kb$, $kb$log a call$kb$, $kb$agent floor$kb$]::text[], 'mediflow_guide', true, false),
($kb$lib-mf-quoting-engine$kb$, $kb$mf-quoting-engine$kb$, $kb$Mediflow Guide: Sales Tools$kb$, $kb$Quoting Engine: what works today and what is not connected$kb$, $kb$Where: Sales Tools > Quoting Engine (Super Admin, Agency Admin, Compliance Manager, Agent Support).

Important: Mediflow does not have plan, premium, formulary or star-rating data loaded. The Plan Comparison tab shows no plans, and the Compare plans button is disabled. It never shows sample prices. Do not use it to quote real premiums or drug costs.

What does work:
- Inputs: ZIP code, plan type (Medicare Advantage, Part D, Medigap) and a list of drugs (type a name, press Enter). These stay on the screen only and are not saved to a client record.
- Provider Network tab: doctor lookup from the public CMS NPPES NPI Registry. Enter at least two letters of the last name; first name, state and ZIP are optional. Results show specialty, NPI and address, with Add to quote. It does not say whether a doctor is in a plan's network; that needs carrier network data that is not connected.
- Your carriers card: lists active carriers, with Manage (Admin > Carriers).
- Formulary Lookup tab: lists the drugs you added, marked as needing plan data.

The page says it is waiting on CMS plan landscape files, formulary files, provider networks and your carrier list. A disclaimer on the page reminds users that only plans the agency offers are shown.$kb$, ARRAY[$kb$quoting$kb$, $kb$quote$kb$, $kb$plan comparison$kb$, $kb$formulary$kb$, $kb$drug$kb$, $kb$doctor lookup$kb$, $kb$npi$kb$, $kb$provider network$kb$, $kb$premium$kb$, $kb$medicare advantage$kb$, $kb$medigap$kb$, $kb$part d$kb$, $kb$compare plans$kb$]::text[], 'mediflow_guide', true, false),
($kb$lib-mf-aep-center$kb$, $kb$mf-aep-center$kb$, $kb$Mediflow Guide: Sales Tools$kb$, $kb$AEP Center: annual review readiness$kb$, $kb$Where: Sales Tools > AEP Center (Super Admin, Agency Admin, Compliance Manager). The page is read-only reporting; it has no buttons to change anything.

What it counts: current members, meaning contacts with status Enrolled or Retained whose current plan type is MA or MAPD. For each one, Mediflow creates a task to set the annual review appointment. Mediflow is set up to create these automatically once a year on Sept 1 (the agent must have a linked user), and an admin can also run it on demand through the system. Running it again does not create duplicates.

What you see:
- Tiles: Members to review, Reviews in progress, Reviews completed, Overdue.
- Review coverage: members who have a review task, and how many do not.
- Review completion: tasks marked done.
- Season key dates: Mediflow is set up to show Sept 30 (set reviews by), Oct 1 (new plan details), Oct 15 to Dec 7 (AEP window) and Jan 1 renewal. These dates are built into the page, not looked up.
- Review progress by agent: total, done, open and overdue for each agent.

To work a review, open the task on Main > Tasks. Mark it done when finished and the numbers here update. Members with no review task, or no assigned agent, show up as a coverage gap.$kb$, ARRAY[$kb$aep$kb$, $kb$annual enrollment$kb$, $kb$aep center$kb$, $kb$renewal$kb$, $kb$annual review$kb$, $kb$review task$kb$, $kb$members to review$kb$, $kb$overdue$kb$, $kb$coverage$kb$, $kb$ma$kb$, $kb$mapd$kb$, $kb$enrollment period$kb$]::text[], 'mediflow_guide', true, false),
($kb$lib-mf-ready-to-sell$kb$, $kb$mf-ready-to-sell$kb$, $kb$Mediflow Guide: Sales Tools$kb$, $kb$Ready to Sell: agent readiness board$kb$, $kb$Where: Sales Tools > Ready to Sell (Super Admin, Agency Admin, Compliance Manager).

Purpose: shows which agents can take routed calls and sell, and what is blocking the rest. It uses the same rules as inbound lead routing.

An agent is Ready when ALL are true: status is active; AHIP is current (passed or waived for the certification year); at least one active, unexpired state license; at least one passed or waived, unexpired carrier certification for that year.

The board:
- Tiles: Ready to sell, Not ready yet, Expiring within 7 days, Expiring within 30 days.
- Agent readiness table: name and NPN, a Ready or Not ready badge, AHIP (Current or Missing), count of licensed states, count of certified carriers, and Blockers.
- Blocker labels: Inactive; AHIP not current; No active state license; State license expired; No carrier certifications.
- Switch Not ready only to hide ready agents.
- Expiring soon: licenses and certifications about to run out, within 30, 60 or 90 days. Renew them before the agent stops receiving routed calls.

To fix a blocker, update the agent's record (Management > Agents) or their Licensing and Certifications. This page does not edit anything.$kb$, ARRAY[$kb$ready to sell$kb$, $kb$readiness$kb$, $kb$agent readiness$kb$, $kb$ahip$kb$, $kb$license$kb$, $kb$certification$kb$, $kb$blocker$kb$, $kb$expiring$kb$, $kb$routable$kb$, $kb$not ready$kb$, $kb$carrier certification$kb$]::text[], 'mediflow_guide', true, false),
($kb$lib-mf-policies$kb$, $kb$mf-policies$kb$, $kb$Mediflow Guide: Sales Tools$kb$, $kb$Policies: the agency's book of business$kb$, $kb$Where: Main > Policies (Super Admin, Agency Admin, Compliance Manager, Agent Support). Agents see a client's policies through Main > My Clients.

What it is: a list of every plan your clients are enrolled in, from the enrollments records. Columns: Policy #, Client (click to open the client), Carrier, Plan type, Status, Effectuated, Effective date and Agent.

Top tiles: Active policies, Waiting on the carrier (pending), Effectuated, and Starting in 60 days. Tiles follow your filters, so the totals match the list.

Filters: search by client or policy number, Status (Active, Pending, Terminated, Cancelled, Declined), Plan type, Carrier, Agent, Effectuated or not, and an effective date range. Clear filters resets them.

Export CSV downloads the book (Super Admin, Agency Admin, Compliance Manager, Agent Support). Import and Export has a Policies tab for spreadsheet import.

Limits: premium and per-policy commission are not tracked here (see Commissions). I found no Add Policy button on this page or on the client page; the empty-state text suggests recording a plan on a client's page or importing. The Applications tab on a client shows enrollment applications received from EnrollHere/Sunfire.$kb$, ARRAY[$kb$policies$kb$, $kb$policy$kb$, $kb$enrollment$kb$, $kb$book of business$kb$, $kb$effectuated$kb$, $kb$carrier$kb$, $kb$plan type$kb$, $kb$effective date$kb$, $kb$export policies$kb$, $kb$pending$kb$, $kb$terminated$kb$]::text[], 'mediflow_guide', true, false),
($kb$lib-mf-tasks-calendar$kb$, $kb$mf-tasks-calendar$kb$, $kb$Mediflow Guide: Sales Tools$kb$, $kb$Tasks and Calendar & Appointments$kb$, $kb$TASKS. Where: Main > Tasks (all roles). A red badge on the sidebar item shows overdue tasks.
- Tiles show To do, In progress and Done counts. Search or filter by status.
- Click the circle next to a task to complete or reopen it. Overdue tasks show a red due date.
- New Task (Super Admin, Agency Admin, Compliance Manager, Agent Support): title, details, due date, priority (low, medium, high, urgent).
- Templates tab (same roles, not agents): save reusable tasks, optionally with an automatic trigger such as Agent Created or License Expiring (30d). From Template creates a task from one.
- Agents see only their own tasks and can only change status; they cannot create tasks.
- AEP review tasks made by Mediflow appear here too.

CALENDAR. Where: Main > Calendar (all roles). Shows appointments only, not tasks. Switch Month, Week or Agenda, use Today and the arrows, and filter by agent. Tiles count Total, Confirmed, Pending, Completed.
- Book appointment (Super Admin, Agency Admin, Compliance Manager, Agent Support, Agent): title, client, type (Enrollment, Review, Renewal, Consultation, Other), status, date, start, length, agent, where (Office, Phone, Video call, Home visit), notes. The form says clients with a phone or email get a reminder the day before unless opted out.
- Only Super Admin, Agency Admin and Agents can delete one.
- Google and Outlook sync is marked Coming soon.$kb$, ARRAY[$kb$tasks$kb$, $kb$to do$kb$, $kb$task$kb$, $kb$overdue$kb$, $kb$template$kb$, $kb$calendar$kb$, $kb$appointment$kb$, $kb$book appointment$kb$, $kb$schedule$kb$, $kb$reminder$kb$, $kb$agenda$kb$, $kb$priority$kb$, $kb$due date$kb$]::text[], 'mediflow_guide', true, false),
($kb$lib-mf-documents$kb$, $kb$mf-documents$kb$, $kb$Mediflow Guide: Client Service & Back Office$kb$, $kb$Documents: storing and downloading agent files$kb$, $kb$Where: sidebar > Clients & Service > Documents. The menu item shows for every role, but the page only loads for roles allowed to view agent records (Agency Admin, Compliance Manager, Agent Support, Viewer). The Agent role is not allowed in.

What it is: one place for each agent's files, such as contracts, E&O certificates, licenses, compliance and training documents. Categories: Contract, E&O Certificate, Compliance, License, Training, Other.

To upload (Agency Admin or Compliance Manager only):
1. Click Upload document.
2. Pick the agent, pick a category, choose the file.
3. Click upload. The file is sent to private storage and listed on the page.

To find a file: filter by agent or by category, then use the Download icon on its row.
To remove one: click the trash icon and confirm. The page warns that this cannot be undone. Only Agency Admin and Compliance Manager can delete.

Access: you only see your own agency's files. A download is checked against your agency before it starts, and files are not public. Agent Support and Viewer can see and download but cannot upload or delete. Documents filed against a client also show on that client's Client Portal preview.$kb$, ARRAY[$kb$documents$kb$, $kb$upload$kb$, $kb$download$kb$, $kb$contract$kb$, $kb$e&o$kb$, $kb$certificate$kb$, $kb$license$kb$, $kb$files$kb$, $kb$storage$kb$, $kb$agent documents$kb$, $kb$delete document$kb$]::text[], 'mediflow_guide', true, false),
($kb$lib-mf-workflow-automation$kb$, $kb$mf-workflow-automation$kb$, $kb$Mediflow Guide: Client Service & Back Office$kb$, $kb$Workflow Automation: rules that run on their own$kb$, $kb$Where: sidebar > Sales Tools > Workflow Automation (Agency Admin and Super Admin). Only they can create, edit, run or delete rules.

A rule reads as a sentence: when this happens, do these steps.

To build one: click New rule, name it, pick "When this happens" (some need a number of days), optionally add "Only if" conditions, then add actions in order.

Triggers: new lead; lead status changes; new client; client status changes; client assigned; client gone quiet (N days); deal moves stage; task overdue (N days); task completed; license expiring (within N days); certification expiring; AHIP deadline; enrollment period opens; commission received; commission missed; chargeback received; weekly check.

Conditions (is, is not, contains, more than, less than, is filled in) on: status, lead source, assigned agent, state, carrier, days until expiry, days since last contact, days overdue, old/new status.

Actions: create task, in-app alert, send email, send text, update client status, start a follow-up sequence, move deal stage, book appointment. Message text can use placeholders like {{first_name}}.

On each rule: a switch pauses it; Run now, Edit, Delete. Recent runs refresh every 30 seconds. Client texts and emails are checked against opt-outs, consent and texting hours, and skipped if the client cannot be messaged. Saving rules needs two-step verification on your account.$kb$, ARRAY[$kb$workflow$kb$, $kb$automation$kb$, $kb$rules$kb$, $kb$trigger$kb$, $kb$condition$kb$, $kb$action$kb$, $kb$auto task$kb$, $kb$automatic text$kb$, $kb$automatic email$kb$, $kb$sequence$kb$, $kb$if then$kb$, $kb$run now$kb$]::text[], 'mediflow_guide', true, false),
($kb$lib-mf-reports$kb$, $kb$mf-reports$kb$, $kb$Mediflow Guide: Client Service & Back Office$kb$, $kb$Reports: dashboards and CSV downloads$kb$, $kb$Where: sidebar > Management > Reports (Agency Admin, Compliance Manager, Agent Support). Page title: Reporting & Analytics.

Tabs: Report library, Executive, Agent Performance, Pipeline, Lead Sources, Compliance Matrix, Communications, Retention.

Report library: seven reports, each downloaded as a CSV spreadsheet with the Run button. Dated reports (Executive summary, Agent production, Pipeline & win rate, Lead sources, Communications) use the date range you pick at the top; the options include last 30, 60, 90 days, 6 months and a year. Compliance status and Retention & churn show the situation right now.

The other tabs show the same data on screen (counts, charts, trends) with an Export CSV button.

Who can do what:
- Executive tab and its export: Agency Admin only.
- Compliance Matrix (licenses by state, expirations, carrier certifications): Agency Admin and Compliance Manager.
- Other tabs can be viewed by all four roles above. Their CSV exports are for Agency Admin and Compliance Manager.

Exports require that you signed in within the last 15 minutes. If you see a message asking you to refresh your session, reload the page, sign in again and retry. Exports are logged. Reports are agency-wide numbers; nothing is scheduled or emailed automatically.$kb$, ARRAY[$kb$reports$kb$, $kb$analytics$kb$, $kb$export$kb$, $kb$csv$kb$, $kb$executive$kb$, $kb$agent performance$kb$, $kb$pipeline$kb$, $kb$lead sources$kb$, $kb$compliance matrix$kb$, $kb$communications$kb$, $kb$retention report$kb$, $kb$download$kb$]::text[], 'mediflow_guide', true, false),
($kb$lib-mf-client-portal$kb$, $kb$mf-client-portal$kb$, $kb$Mediflow Guide: Client Service & Back Office$kb$, $kb$Client Portal: staff preview of the client view$kb$, $kb$Where: sidebar > Clients & Service > Client Portal (Agency Admin and Super Admin).

Important: this is a preview for staff. Clients cannot log in yet; the page says client logins are coming soon. Nothing here is a live client-facing site.

What it does: shows what one client would see in a future self-service portal, built from real data on their record.

Steps:
1. Open Client Portal.
2. Search for a client by name, phone or email.
3. Review the preview.

Sections: My Plan (enrollments with carrier, plan type and year; if none, the plan recorded on the client), Messages (the latest 50 texts and emails with the client, oldest first), Documents (files filed against the client, with a download icon), Upcoming Appointments, and Contact Agent (the assigned agent). The "Schedule New Appointment" and contact buttons are shown as coming soon and are disabled.

Replying: below Messages you can send a text or email. This is turned off if your role cannot send messages, or if the client opted out of that channel or has no phone or email.

Privacy: every time you open a client's preview, Mediflow records it in the audit log first; if that record cannot be saved, nothing is shown. Sensitive fields such as the Medicare ID and date of birth are masked for roles that are not cleared to see them, and health conditions are not part of the preview.$kb$, ARRAY[$kb$client portal$kb$, $kb$portal$kb$, $kb$preview$kb$, $kb$client view$kb$, $kb$self-service$kb$, $kb$member portal$kb$, $kb$client login$kb$, $kb$messages$kb$, $kb$my plan$kb$, $kb$beneficiary$kb$]::text[], 'mediflow_guide', true, false),
($kb$lib-mf-campaigns-sequences$kb$, $kb$mf-campaigns-sequences$kb$, $kb$Mediflow Guide: Client Service & Back Office$kb$, $kb$Omnichannel Campaigns and drip sequences$kb$, $kb$Where: sidebar > Sales Tools > Omnichannel Campaigns (Agency Admin, Compliance Manager, Agent Support, Super Admin). Tabs: Campaigns, Templates, Tracking, Unsubscribes (SMS Opt-Outs on the text channel), Drip Sequences. Switch between Email and SMS at the top.

Who can do what: everyone above can view. Agency Admin and Agent Support can build drafts. Only Agency Admin can send, schedule, cancel or delete, change sender settings, or re-subscribe an email address.

Build a campaign: name it, optionally start from a template, write the subject and message (merge fields: {{first_name}}, {{last_name}}, {{agency_name}}, {{agent_name}}, {{plan_type}}, {{carrier}}, {{plan_year}}). Choose the audience by status, plan type, carrier, state, lead source, tag or birthday month; a live count shows who will receive it. Save as draft, then send now or schedule within 90 days.

Built-in protections: clients marked do not contact, without an address, or opted out are left out automatically. Email needs a mailing address in settings and unsubscribe links set up; SMS needs Twilio connected. If something is missing, sending is blocked with a message.

Drip Sequences: ordered steps (text, email, task, wait) with delays in minutes, hours or days. Enroll clients by hand or with a workflow rule action. Trigger labels like birthday do not enroll anyone automatically.$kb$, ARRAY[$kb$campaign$kb$, $kb$email$kb$, $kb$sms$kb$, $kb$text$kb$, $kb$drip$kb$, $kb$sequence$kb$, $kb$template$kb$, $kb$audience$kb$, $kb$unsubscribe$kb$, $kb$opt-out$kb$, $kb$stop$kb$, $kb$schedule$kb$, $kb$blast$kb$, $kb$marketing$kb$]::text[], 'mediflow_guide', true, false),
($kb$lib-mf-retention-churn$kb$, $kb$mf-retention-churn$kb$, $kb$Mediflow Guide: Client Service & Back Office$kb$, $kb$Retention & Churn Risk: who might leave$kb$, $kb$Where: sidebar > Clients & Service > Retention & Churn Risk (Agency Admin, Compliance Manager, Super Admin).

What it shows: every current member (clients with status Enrolled or Retained, up to 2,000) with a risk score from 0 to 100, ranked so you can call the riskiest first. Click a member to open their record.

How the score is built (a simple points total, capped at 100):
- No contact on record or 90+ days: 35 points; 60 to 89 days: 18.
- Open or investigating complaint: 25.
- Open at-risk flag from the retention team: 25.
- First plan renewal (plan year is last year): 15.
Bands: High 50 and up, Medium 25 to 49, Low below 25. Each member lists the reasons. Health and race answers are never used.

Page layout: four cards (High, Medium, Low, average score; click one to filter) and a reference card of Medicare election periods (AEP Oct 15 to Dec 7, OEP Jan 1 to Mar 31, SEP with a qualifying event).

Related lists: Clients & Leads > Retention tab shows birthdays in the next 30 days, clients with no contact in 60+ days, and an AEP review list (enrolled, retained and prospect clients). Reports > Retention shows enrolled, at-risk and lost members. You can also start a workflow rule on "Client gone quiet".$kb$, ARRAY[$kb$retention$kb$, $kb$churn$kb$, $kb$risk$kb$, $kb$at risk$kb$, $kb$lapse$kb$, $kb$disenroll$kb$, $kb$renewal$kb$, $kb$aep$kb$, $kb$oep$kb$, $kb$birthday$kb$, $kb$no contact$kb$, $kb$score$kb$, $kb$keep clients$kb$]::text[], 'mediflow_guide', true, false),
($kb$lib-mf-knowledge-base$kb$, $kb$mf-knowledge-base$kb$, $kb$Mediflow Guide: Client Service & Back Office$kb$, $kb$Knowledge Base: your articles and the Mediflow library$kb$, $kb$Where: sidebar > Clients & Service > Knowledge Base. Two views: "Our articles" (written by your agency) and "Mediflow library" (shared by Mediflow with every agency). All staff can read. Only Agency Admin and Super Admin can add, edit, switch on/off or delete.

Our articles (owners): click Add article, fill in Category, Title, the text and Keywords separated by commas (for example: aep, switching), leave "Switched on" selected, then click Add article. Use the switch on a row to turn one off or on. You can search by title, text or keyword and filter by category.

Mediflow library: ready-made guides on how Mediflow works are on by default. General Medicare notes are off by default and marked "Check before using", because they were written in 2025 and some figures or rules may be out of date. Each agency chooses for itself with the switch on each article (or "switch on/off all shown"). Your choices never affect other agencies.

The AI assistant: when someone asks it a question, Mediflow looks at your own switched-on articles AND the library articles you have switched on, matching the question against keywords, titles and text (keywords count most). It gives the best three to the assistant as reference notes, at most 1,500 characters from each, and treats them as facts, not instructions.

Tips: keep your own articles short, put the words people will type in the keywords, and never put client names, Medicare IDs or other client information in an article.$kb$, ARRAY[$kb$knowledge base$kb$, $kb$kb$kb$, $kb$articles$kb$, $kb$assistant$kb$, $kb$ai$kb$, $kb$notes$kb$, $kb$keywords$kb$, $kb$switch on$kb$, $kb$add article$kb$, $kb$reference$kb$, $kb$how-to$kb$, $kb$faq$kb$]::text[], 'mediflow_guide', true, false),
($kb$lib-mf-team-invitations$kb$, $kb$mf-team-invitations$kb$, $kb$Mediflow Guide: Client Service & Back Office$kb$, $kb$Team: inviting people and managing seats$kb$, $kb$Where: sidebar > Admin > Team (Agency Admin and Super Admin). Page title: Team.

Seats: each person who can sign in uses one seat. An invitation that has not been accepted also uses a seat.

To invite someone:
1. Click Invite member.
2. Enter their email and choose a role: Agent, Agent Support, Compliance Manager, Viewer or Agency Admin. Super Admin cannot be given by invitation.
3. Send. The invitation link works for 7 days.
If no seats are free, the Invite button is disabled. If email is not set up, Mediflow shows the link once so you can copy and send it yourself ("Link copied").

For a pending invitation (listed as "Invited, not yet accepted" with its expiry):
- Resend creates a new link and the old one stops working.
- Revoke cancels it and frees the seat.

For existing members:
- Deactivate stops their access and frees the seat.
- Reactivate brings them back, if a seat is free.

You cannot invite an email that is already a member or already has a pending invitation; Mediflow will tell you.

Related: Management > Agents lists agents with their licenses and compliance. Add Agent creates the agent record and starts their onboarding checklist. An agent record is separate from a login; to let the agent sign in, invite them here with the Agent role.$kb$, ARRAY[$kb$team$kb$, $kb$invite$kb$, $kb$invitation$kb$, $kb$seat$kb$, $kb$user$kb$, $kb$role$kb$, $kb$deactivate$kb$, $kb$reactivate$kb$, $kb$add user$kb$, $kb$member$kb$, $kb$revoke$kb$, $kb$resend$kb$]::text[], 'mediflow_guide', true, false),
($kb$lib-mf-agent-contracting$kb$, $kb$mf-agent-contracting$kb$, $kb$Mediflow Guide: Client Service & Back Office$kb$, $kb$Agent contracting and onboarding with carriers$kb$, $kb$Admin side: sidebar > Management > Contracting (Agency Admin, Compliance Manager, Super Admin).
Agent side: sidebar > Main > My Onboarding (Agent role).

Steps:
1. Admin clicks Start new onboarding and picks an agent (not offboarded). If a run is open already, it opens that one.
2. The agent works through the wizard: Welcome, Your profile, Carriers, Review, Authorize, Sign, Done. Answers save as they go. SSN and EIN are encrypted, and masked for roles not cleared to see them.
3. The agent picks the carriers they want. The run then waits for admin review.
4. An admin opens the run and clicks "Review and request contracting" to generate the paperwork. Admins can also Cancel onboarding.
5. Authorize step: the agent chooses either to let the agency handle carrier submissions (they sign one power of attorney) or to finish each carrier themselves (invite requests are queued to the carriers; going back later needs an admin to cancel and restart).
6. For each carrier request, an admin clicks Mark submitted, then records the writing number once the carrier appoints the agent; saving it marks the appointment complete.

Filter runs by status: Draft, Profile in progress, Awaiting admin review, Signing paperwork, Submitted, Complete, Cancelled. Mediflow creates tasks for the agent and admins along the way.$kb$, ARRAY[$kb$contracting$kb$, $kb$onboarding$kb$, $kb$carrier$kb$, $kb$appointment$kb$, $kb$writing number$kb$, $kb$poa$kb$, $kb$power of attorney$kb$, $kb$sign$kb$, $kb$agent$kb$, $kb$new agent$kb$, $kb$profile$kb$, $kb$paperwork$kb$]::text[], 'mediflow_guide', true, false),
($kb$lib-mf-import-export$kb$, $kb$mf-import-export$kb$, $kb$Mediflow Guide: Client Service & Back Office$kb$, $kb$Import, export and data migration$kb$, $kb$Where: sidebar > Admin > Import / Export (Agency Admin and Super Admin). Imports run in the wizard at Import & Migration (reached from the Import buttons); both are admin only.

EXPORT: three CSV downloads of your whole book: clients, policies and agents (up to 25,000 rows each). Click Export on the card. Medicare IDs are never included, and dates of birth and health conditions are left out. The agent export has no SSN, EIN or contracting data. You must have signed in within the last 15 minutes; if asked, sign in again and retry. Every export is recorded in the audit log.

IMPORT sources:
- Agents from Monday.com (board export CSV).
- Contacts from GoHighLevel (CSV). On duplicates choose Skip, Merge fields or Create new record.
- Clients from any CSV, including Medicare ID, carrier, plan and effective date; rows with plan details also create an enrollment. Medicare IDs are encrypted when saved. If the person already exists choose Fill in blanks + add coverage, Skip the row, or Create a separate contact.

Wizard steps: Upload (CSV, up to 50 MB), Map Fields (match your columns), Validate (every row is checked before anything saves), Import (progress bar). Rows with problems are listed.

After an import, Import history lists each job; download the errors CSV for rows that failed, fix them and import again. The Import / Export page also shows recent imports.$kb$, ARRAY[$kb$import$kb$, $kb$export$kb$, $kb$migration$kb$, $kb$csv$kb$, $kb$monday$kb$, $kb$gohighlevel$kb$, $kb$ghl$kb$, $kb$spreadsheet$kb$, $kb$upload clients$kb$, $kb$backup$kb$, $kb$duplicates$kb$, $kb$map fields$kb$, $kb$data tools$kb$]::text[], 'mediflow_guide', true, false),
($kb$lib-mf-commissions-overview$kb$, $kb$mf-commissions-overview$kb$, $kb$Mediflow Guide: Commissions & Carriers$kb$, $kb$Commissions page (agency view) and My Commissions (agent view)$kb$, $kb$WHERE: Sidebar group Commissions. "Commissions" is visible to Super Admin, Agency Admin, Compliance Manager and Agent Support. "My Commissions" is visible to the Agent role only.

COMMISSIONS (agency): Four cards for one month: Earned, Paid out, Waiting to be paid, Missed payments. The month is the latest with agent payouts. Four tabs:
- Statements: carrier statements and their status (Pending, Parsed, Reconciled, Reconciled with variance). Click a row to open it.
- Schedules: rate cards per carrier, plan type and year (initial %, renewal %, flat $).
- Hierarchies: upline splits (writing agent, upline agent, split %, effective dates). When a statement is reconciled, the upline gets that % of each line and the writing agent keeps the rest.
- Missed payments: expected commissions that never showed up. Click Resolve and add a note.
Uploading statements is Super Admin / Agency Admin only and requires MFA (see the upload article).

MARK AN AGENT PAID: Management > Agents > open the agent > Commissions tab > Mark paid (admins only, MFA required).

MY COMMISSIONS (agent): shows only your own pay periods, newest first, with Period, Amount, Status and Paid date. "Paid to you" adds up periods marked paid; "On its way" adds up everything else (open, approved or held). If you see "commission account isn't set up", ask your agency admin to link your profile.$kb$, ARRAY[$kb$commissions$kb$, $kb$my commissions$kb$, $kb$commission statement$kb$, $kb$payout$kb$, $kb$paid$kb$, $kb$earned$kb$, $kb$pending$kb$, $kb$rate card$kb$, $kb$schedule$kb$, $kb$upline$kb$, $kb$hierarchy$kb$, $kb$split$kb$, $kb$override$kb$, $kb$mark paid$kb$]::text[], 'mediflow_guide', true, false),
($kb$lib-mf-commission-statement-upload$kb$, $kb$mf-commission-statement-upload$kb$, $kb$Mediflow Guide: Commissions & Carriers$kb$, $kb$Uploading carrier commission statements: supported carriers, formats and bad rows$kb$, $kb$WHERE: Commissions > Upload statement button, or Reconciliation > Upload statement. Only Super Admin and Agency Admin can upload, and MFA must be on.

STEPS: 1) Choose the carrier, statement date, period start/end, total (required) and the file. 2) Submit. The statement is created as Pending, then Mediflow tries to read (parse) it. 3) A Parsed statement shows a Reconcile button.

SUPPORTED CARRIERS: Mediflow has readers for Humana (pipe-delimited, no header row), UnitedHealthcare/AARP (CSV, no header), Aetna/CVS (CSV with a header row; needs Member ID and Commission Amount columns) and Anthem/BCBS (CSV, no header). The reader is chosen by the carrier's NAME (containing Humana, UHC, AARP, Aetna, CVS, Anthem, BCBS or Blue Cross). Other carriers (Cigna, Wellcare, etc.) have no reader: the parse is refused with "No parser registered". The picker lists PDF/XLSX/XLS, but readers handle only CSV/text.

BAD ROWS: For Humana, UHC and Anthem, rows with fewer than 12 columns or entirely blank are silently skipped, and not reported. Unreadable amounts become $0.00. Amounts in parentheses, like (500.00), are read as negative. Types CHGBK, CB, charge, recoup, reverse become chargebacks.

KNOWN ISSUE: Mediflow does not keep the uploaded file. The on-screen Parse step does not re-send it, so a statement can stay Pending with no lines and show "parse failed". Tell your admin.$kb$, ARRAY[$kb$upload$kb$, $kb$statement$kb$, $kb$commission statement$kb$, $kb$csv$kb$, $kb$parse$kb$, $kb$parser$kb$, $kb$humana$kb$, $kb$unitedhealthcare$kb$, $kb$aetna$kb$, $kb$anthem$kb$, $kb$carrier file$kb$, $kb$bad rows$kb$, $kb$pending$kb$, $kb$no parser registered$kb$]::text[], 'mediflow_guide', true, false),
($kb$lib-mf-commission-reconciliation$kb$, $kb$mf-commission-reconciliation$kb$, $kb$Mediflow Guide: Commissions & Carriers$kb$, $kb$Reconciliation: how statement lines are matched and what variance means$kb$, $kb$WHERE: Sidebar group Commissions > Reconciliation. Visible to Super Admin, Agency Admin, Compliance Manager and Agent Support.

HOW MATCHING WORKS: On a Parsed statement, click Reconcile (on the list row or the statement page). For each line Mediflow: 1) looks for a client whose Medicare ID matches the line's Member ID; 2) if none, tries last name + date of birth (+ state when given); 3) finds the writing agent from the client's assigned agent, or else the client's earliest deal owner. A line with both a client and an agent is Matched; otherwise it is "Needs a match". Matched lines are credited to the agent's pay period, with upline splits applied.

FIX UNMATCHED LINES: Open the statement (or use the Unmatched lines tab), click Match on a line, pick a contact and writing agent, Save. It is then "Matched by hand". The payout is only recalculated when Reconcile runs again, which the screen only offers while a statement is Parsed.

STATUSES: Pending = uploaded, not read. Parsed = read, ready to reconcile. Reconciled = matched and paid out. Reconciled with variance = reconciled, but the carrier's stated total differs from the sum of its lines by $0.01 or more; the page shows the difference. Disputed is never set today.

Disputes & aging, 1099 rollup and GL export tabs say Coming soon and do nothing yet.$kb$, ARRAY[$kb$reconciliation$kb$, $kb$reconcile$kb$, $kb$variance$kb$, $kb$unmatched$kb$, $kb$match$kb$, $kb$matched by hand$kb$, $kb$statement total$kb$, $kb$missed payments$kb$, $kb$needs a match$kb$, $kb$reconciled with variance$kb$, $kb$difference$kb$, $kb$carrier statement$kb$, $kb$does not add up$kb$]::text[], 'mediflow_guide', true, false),
($kb$lib-mf-missed-payments$kb$, $kb$mf-missed-payments$kb$, $kb$Mediflow Guide: Commissions & Carriers$kb$, $kb$Missed payments: how Mediflow flags commissions that never arrived$kb$, $kb$WHERE: Commissions > Missed payments tab, and Reconciliation > Missed payments tab. Same roles as Commissions (Super Admin, Agency Admin, Compliance Manager, Agent Support). Resolving is Super Admin / Agency Admin only, with MFA.

HOW IT WORKS: A nightly check (02:30 UTC) looks at every active, effectuated enrollment (not lost or do-not-contact clients). If no commission line item for that policy turned up for last calendar month within the last 60 days, Mediflow adds an alert. It checks per policy, so a client with an MA plan and a separate PDP can have two alerts.

EXPECTED AMOUNT: Mediflow looks up the active rate card for that carrier, plan type and plan year. The Expected $ is filled in only when the rate card has a flat dollar amount. If the card uses only percentages, the amount is left blank. Mediflow does not compute it from premium.

WHAT YOU SEE: Contact, policy number, expected amount, expected period and days overdue (amber at 30 days, red at 60).

STEPS TO CLOSE ONE: Click Resolve, optionally type a note (for example, that the carrier confirmed payment next cycle), and confirm. A resolved alert leaves the list and cannot be re-resolved. Resolving does not change any payout.

TIP: Add rate cards on the Schedules tab. Without one, alerts still appear but with no amount.$kb$, ARRAY[$kb$missed payment$kb$, $kb$missed commission$kb$, $kb$expected commission$kb$, $kb$overdue$kb$, $kb$alert$kb$, $kb$resolve$kb$, $kb$rate card$kb$, $kb$schedule$kb$, $kb$never arrived$kb$, $kb$not paid$kb$, $kb$carrier did not pay$kb$, $kb$days overdue$kb$]::text[], 'mediflow_guide', true, false),
($kb$lib-mf-clawbacks$kb$, $kb$mf-clawbacks$kb$, $kb$Mediflow Guide: Commissions & Carriers$kb$, $kb$Clawbacks (chargebacks): what the Clawbacks page shows$kb$, $kb$WHERE: Sidebar group Commissions > Clawbacks. Visible to Super Admin, Agency Admin, Compliance Manager and Agent Support. It is a read-only report; there is nothing to edit or dispute on it.

WHAT IT IS: A clawback is commission a carrier takes back, usually when a member leaves a plan early. Mediflow does not detect clawbacks itself. They appear only when an uploaded carrier statement has a line classed as a chargeback (type CHGBK, CB, or text containing charge, recoup or reverse).

WHAT YOU CAN DO: Pick a window at the top: Last 90 days, Last 12 months (default) or Last 24 months. You see four cards: Clawed back (total dollars), Chargebacks (count), Clawback rate (clawed back as a share of gross commission), and Gross commission (non-chargeback lines). Below are Exposure by agent (who has the most clawed back, biggest first; "Unassigned" when no writing agent is linked) and Recent chargebacks (policy, member, agent, period, amount, newest first, up to 500).

HOW THE PAYOUT IS AFFECTED: When a statement with chargebacks is reconciled and a line is matched to an agent, the negative amount is subtracted from that agent's earned total for the period, including any upline split.

TIPS: Unmatched chargeback lines show as Unassigned and do not reduce any agent until matched and reconciled. The window is based on the line's period start date.$kb$, ARRAY[$kb$clawback$kb$, $kb$clawbacks$kb$, $kb$chargeback$kb$, $kb$chargebacks$kb$, $kb$disenrollment$kb$, $kb$early disenroll$kb$, $kb$commission taken back$kb$, $kb$recoup$kb$, $kb$clawback rate$kb$, $kb$exposure$kb$, $kb$negative commission$kb$]::text[], 'mediflow_guide', true, false),
($kb$lib-mf-carrier-connectors$kb$, $kb$mf-carrier-connectors$kb$, $kb$Mediflow Guide: Commissions & Carriers$kb$, $kb$Carrier connectors: what Mediflow really connects to (and what it does not)$kb$, $kb$SHORT ANSWER: Mediflow has no live connection to any carrier's systems. There is no carrier API, portal login, SOAP feed or automatic commission download. Commission data enters only when an admin uploads a statement file.

WHAT EXISTS: A "connector" in Mediflow is only for agent contracting (appointment) paperwork, not commissions. The one working connector is Email (appointment desk). When an agent's signed contracting packet is ready, Mediflow emails it, with the signed PDF attached, to the carrier's appointment-desk address you set on the Carriers page, optionally CCing your list and using your subject line. It sends for real through the email service. If a carrier has no desk email, or email sending is not configured, it does NOT pretend to have sent; the request stays open and retries once fixed.

NO STATUS FEEDBACK: Email is fire-and-forget. Mediflow cannot ask the carrier for status, so carrier replies (acknowledged, appointed, rejected) are tracked by a person updating the request, not automatically.

NOT BUILT YET: Native connectors for individual carriers (code comments mention a future Aetna connector) are planned only. Nothing is registered today, and the screens do not show a connector status. A server-side rehearsal mode (dry run) exists for testing and sends nothing.

SEE ALSO: Carriers admin page article; Uploading carrier commission statements article.$kb$, ARRAY[$kb$carrier connector$kb$, $kb$carrier integration$kb$, $kb$carrier api$kb$, $kb$integration$kb$, $kb$appointment desk$kb$, $kb$email connector$kb$, $kb$contracting$kb$, $kb$appointment$kb$, $kb$portal$kb$, $kb$soap$kb$, $kb$aetna api$kb$, $kb$connect to carrier$kb$, $kb$automatic commission feed$kb$]::text[], 'mediflow_guide', true, false),
($kb$lib-mf-carriers-admin$kb$, $kb$mf-carriers-admin$kb$, $kb$Mediflow Guide: Commissions & Carriers$kb$, $kb$Carriers admin page: add and edit carriers and appointment-desk emails$kb$, $kb$WHERE: Sidebar group Admin > Carriers. Visible to Super Admin and Agency Admin only; other roles see "You don't have access".

WHAT IT IS: The list of carriers your agency sells. New agencies start with these 11 carriers: Humana, UnitedHealth/AARP, Aetna/CVS, Cigna, Anthem/BCBS, Wellcare, Molina, Centene, Devoted, Oscar and Clover. Carriers are also used in statement uploads, rate cards, enrollments and the contracting workflow.

THE PAGE: Four counters (Carriers, Active, Missing a contracting email, Inactive), a search box (name or CMS contract number), and a table: Name, CMS contract #, Active, Appointment desk, Active requests.

STEPS TO ADD: 1) Click Add carrier. 2) Enter the name (required). Optional: CMS contract number (like H1234), logo URL, Active switch. 3) Under appointment desk, enter the desk email, an optional comma-separated CC list and an optional subject template. 4) Save.
TO EDIT: click a row, change fields, Save. To retire a carrier, turn Active off.

IMPORTANT: Mediflow picks its statement reader from the carrier NAME. Keep Humana, UnitedHealth/UHC/AARP, Aetna/CVS or Anthem/BCBS in the name or statement uploads for that carrier will not be readable. Contracting packets for a carrier with no desk email are not sent. There is no delete button on this page, and no connector settings.$kb$, ARRAY[$kb$carriers$kb$, $kb$carrier list$kb$, $kb$add carrier$kb$, $kb$edit carrier$kb$, $kb$appointment desk email$kb$, $kb$cms contract number$kb$, $kb$carrier admin$kb$, $kb$contract number$kb$, $kb$inactive carrier$kb$, $kb$contracting email$kb$, $kb$logo$kb$]::text[], 'mediflow_guide', true, false),
($kb$lib-ab-comm-1$kb$, $kb$ab-comm-1$kb$, $kb$Medicare Commissions$kb$, $kb$How Medicare Advantage commissions work$kb$, $kb$Medicare Advantage (Part C) commissions are paid per enrolled member per year (PEPM). Initial enrollment commissions are typically 3× the renewal rate for the first 12 months, then drop to renewal levels. Commissions are regulated by CMS — carriers cannot pay more than the FMV amounts set annually. Agents must be licensed and appointed with each carrier to receive commissions.$kb$, ARRAY[$kb$commission$kb$, $kb$ma$kb$, $kb$advantage$kb$, $kb$pepm$kb$, $kb$initial$kb$, $kb$renewal$kb$, $kb$payment$kb$, $kb$comp$kb$]::text[], 'medicare_reference', false, true),
($kb$lib-ab-comm-2$kb$, $kb$ab-comm-2$kb$, $kb$Medicare Commissions$kb$, $kb$2025 FMV commission rates (approximate)$kb$, $kb$For 2025, CMS-set FMV commission amounts are approximately $603 for initial Medicare Advantage enrollments and $201 for renewals. Medicare Supplement (Medigap) commissions vary by plan letter and carrier but are generally 20–25% of annual premium for 6–9 years. Part D standalone commissions are capped at ~$103 initial / $51 renewal. Actual amounts vary by carrier and state.$kb$, ARRAY[$kb$fmv$kb$, $kb$rate$kb$, $kb$2025$kb$, $kb$amount$kb$, $kb$supplement$kb$, $kb$medigap$kb$, $kb$part d$kb$, $kb$dollar$kb$]::text[], 'medicare_reference', false, true),
($kb$lib-ab-comm-3$kb$, $kb$ab-comm-3$kb$, $kb$Medicare Commissions$kb$, $kb$Chargeback & clawback rules$kb$, $kb$If a member disenrolls within the first 2–3 months (varies by carrier), the commission is fully clawed back. After the initial clawback window, a pro-rated chargeback may apply if the member leaves mid-year. Chargebacks appear on the agent's commission statement as negative line items. Carriers may also recover advances if the policy lapses.$kb$, ARRAY[$kb$chargeback$kb$, $kb$clawback$kb$, $kb$disenroll$kb$, $kb$lapse$kb$, $kb$recover$kb$, $kb$negative$kb$, $kb$advance$kb$]::text[], 'medicare_reference', false, true),
($kb$lib-ab-comm-4$kb$, $kb$ab-comm-4$kb$, $kb$Medicare Commissions$kb$, $kb$Advance vs. as-earned commission$kb$, $kb$Some carriers offer advanced commission (full year paid upfront within 30–60 days of enrollment) while others pay as-earned (monthly or quarterly). Advances are recouped if the member disenrolls early. New agents often start on as-earned and qualify for advances after a track record. Check each carrier's commission schedule for advance availability.$kb$, ARRAY[$kb$advance$kb$, $kb$as-earned$kb$, $kb$upfront$kb$, $kb$monthly$kb$, $kb$quarterly$kb$, $kb$recoup$kb$, $kb$schedule$kb$]::text[], 'medicare_reference', false, true),
($kb$lib-ab-med-1$kb$, $kb$ab-med-1$kb$, $kb$Medicaid Rules by State$kb$, $kb$Medicaid-Medicare dual eligibles overview$kb$, $kb$Dual eligibles are individuals enrolled in both Medicare and Medicaid. There are two types: Full Benefit Dual Eligibles (FBDE) receive full Medicaid benefits plus Medicare cost-sharing; Qualified Medicare Beneficiaries (QMB) have Medicaid pay premiums and cost-sharing but do not get full Medicaid. States administer Medicaid programs, so eligibility and benefits vary significantly.$kb$, ARRAY[$kb$dual$kb$, $kb$eligible$kb$, $kb$medicaid$kb$, $kb$fbde$kb$, $kb$qmb$kb$, $kb$full benefit$kb$, $kb$state$kb$]::text[], 'medicare_reference', false, true),
($kb$lib-ab-med-2$kb$, $kb$ab-med-2$kb$, $kb$Medicaid Rules by State$kb$, $kb$Medicaid eligibility by income (state variations)$kb$, $kb$Medicaid eligibility income limits vary widely by state. As of 2025, states that expanded Medicaid under ACA cover adults up to 138% FPL. Non-expansion states (e.g., Texas, Florida, Georgia) have much lower limits, often covering only parents, children, disabled, or elderly at very low income thresholds. Always check the specific state's Medicaid agency for current limits. Use the Medicaid.gov state plan finder for authoritative details.$kb$, ARRAY[$kb$income$kb$, $kb$limit$kb$, $kb$fpl$kb$, $kb$expansion$kb$, $kb$non-expansion$kb$, $kb$eligible$kb$, $kb$poverty$kb$, $kb$state$kb$]::text[], 'medicare_reference', false, true),
($kb$lib-ab-med-3$kb$, $kb$ab-med-3$kb$, $kb$Medicaid Rules by State$kb$, $kb$Medicare Savings Programs (MSP) by state$kb$, $kb$Medicare Savings Programs help pay Medicare premiums and cost-sharing. QMB covers Part A & B premiums + cost-sharing (income ≤100% FPL). SLMB covers Part B premiums (120% FPL). QI covers Part B premiums (135% FPL, first-come first-served). Asset limits apply in most states (~$7,970 individual / $11,960 couple for 2025). A few states (e.g., New York, Connecticut) have eliminated asset tests. Income/resource limits vary by state.$kb$, ARRAY[$kb$msp$kb$, $kb$qmb$kb$, $kb$slmb$kb$, $kb$qi$kb$, $kb$savings$kb$, $kb$premium$kb$, $kb$asset$kb$, $kb$resource$kb$, $kb$state$kb$]::text[], 'medicare_reference', false, true),
($kb$lib-ab-med-4$kb$, $kb$ab-med-4$kb$, $kb$Medicaid Rules by State$kb$, $kb$State-specific dual plan (D-SNP) availability$kb$, $kb$Dual-eligible Special Needs Plans (D-SNPs) are available in most states but coverage and benefits vary. Some states coordinate fully with Medicaid (Fully Integrated D-SNPs), others have limited integration. States like California, New York, Texas, and Florida have robust D-SNP markets. Check carrier availability by county — D-SNPs are county-specific. Always verify Medicaid status before enrolling in a D-SNP.$kb$, ARRAY[$kb$d-snp$kb$, $kb$dual$kb$, $kb$integrated$kb$, $kb$county$kb$, $kb$state$kb$, $kb$availability$kb$, $kb$carrier$kb$]::text[], 'medicare_reference', false, true),
($kb$lib-ab-lis-1$kb$, $kb$ab-lis-1$kb$, $kb$Low Income Subsidy (LIS)$kb$, $kb$What is Low Income Subsidy (Extra Help)?$kb$, $kb$The Low Income Subsidy (LIS), also called Extra Help, is a federal program that helps Medicare beneficiaries pay for Part D prescription drug costs — premiums, deductibles, and copays. Full LIS beneficiaries pay no premium (if enrolled in a benchmark plan), no deductible, and low copays ($1.05 generic / $4.15 brand in 2025). Partial LIS beneficiaries get reduced premiums, deductibles, and 15% coinsurance.$kb$, ARRAY[$kb$lis$kb$, $kb$extra help$kb$, $kb$low income$kb$, $kb$subsidy$kb$, $kb$part d$kb$, $kb$premium$kb$, $kb$copay$kb$, $kb$deductible$kb$]::text[], 'medicare_reference', false, true),
($kb$lib-ab-lis-2$kb$, $kb$ab-lis-2$kb$, $kb$Low Income Subsidy (LIS)$kb$, $kb$LIS eligibility income & resource limits (2025)$kb$, $kb$Full LIS: income ≤150% FPL and resources ≤$11,710 individual / $23,410 couple (2025). Partial LIS: income 150–180% FPL, resources ≤$11,710 / $23,410. Those with full Medicaid, SSI, or MSP (QMB/SLMB/QI) automatically qualify for full LIS without a separate application. Apply via SSA Form 1020 or apply online at SSA.gov.$kb$, ARRAY[$kb$lis$kb$, $kb$eligible$kb$, $kb$income$kb$, $kb$resource$kb$, $kb$limit$kb$, $kb$fpl$kb$, $kb$automatic$kb$, $kb$qualify$kb$, $kb$ssa$kb$]::text[], 'medicare_reference', false, true),
($kb$lib-ab-lis-3$kb$, $kb$ab-lis-3$kb$, $kb$Low Income Subsidy (LIS)$kb$, $kb$LIS copay levels and benchmark plans$kb$, $kb$Full LIS beneficiaries at or below 100% FPL pay $1.05 (generic) / $4.15 (brand) copays in 2025. Those between 100–150% FPL pay $4.15 / $10.40. Partial LIS pays 15% coinsurance after deductible. Benchmark plans (lowest-cost plans in a region) have $0 premium for full LIS beneficiaries. If a full LIS beneficiary enrolls in a non-benchmark plan, they may owe a premium.$kb$, ARRAY[$kb$copay$kb$, $kb$benchmark$kb$, $kb$level$kb$, $kb$generic$kb$, $kb$brand$kb$, $kb$coinsurance$kb$, $kb$premium$kb$, $kb$lis$kb$]::text[], 'medicare_reference', false, true),
($kb$lib-ab-lis-4$kb$, $kb$ab-lis-4$kb$, $kb$Low Income Subsidy (LIS)$kb$, $kb$Deemed vs. applied LIS$kb$, $kb$Deemed LIS beneficiaries automatically qualify because they receive Medicaid, SSI, or MSP benefits — no application needed, and they are re-evaluated annually. Applied LIS beneficiaries submitted SSA Form 1020 and may need to reapply if income changes. Deemed status can be verified through the SSA's LIS query or the plan's eligibility file. Always confirm deemed status before plan selection.$kb$, ARRAY[$kb$deemed$kb$, $kb$applied$kb$, $kb$automatic$kb$, $kb$ssi$kb$, $kb$medicaid$kb$, $kb$msp$kb$, $kb$re-evaluate$kb$, $kb$status$kb$]::text[], 'medicare_reference', false, true),
($kb$lib-ab-ma-1$kb$, $kb$ab-ma-1$kb$, $kb$Medicare Advantage Plan Types$kb$, $kb$Types of Medicare Advantage plans$kb$, $kb$Medicare Advantage (Part C) plans include: HMO (Health Maintenance Organization) — requires PCP referrals and in-network care; HMO-POS — HMO with out-of-network flexibility for certain services; PPO (Preferred Provider Organization) — in/out-of-network, no referral needed; PFFS (Private Fee-for-Service) — any provider who accepts terms; SNP (Special Needs Plan) — tailored for chronic conditions, institutional, or dual-eligibles; MSA (Medical Savings Account) — high deductible paired with savings account.$kb$, ARRAY[$kb$hmo$kb$, $kb$ppo$kb$, $kb$pffs$kb$, $kb$snp$kb$, $kb$msa$kb$, $kb$type$kb$, $kb$plan$kb$, $kb$advantage$kb$, $kb$referral$kb$, $kb$network$kb$]::text[], 'medicare_reference', false, true),
($kb$lib-ab-ma-2$kb$, $kb$ab-ma-2$kb$, $kb$Medicare Advantage Plan Types$kb$, $kb$HMO vs PPO key differences$kb$, $kb$HMO plans require members to use in-network providers and typically need PCP referrals for specialists — lower premiums but less flexibility. PPO plans allow in- and out-of-network providers without referrals — higher premiums but more freedom. HMO-POS offers limited out-of-network access for specific services. For beneficiaries who travel frequently or have out-of-area specialists, PPO is usually preferred.$kb$, ARRAY[$kb$hmo$kb$, $kb$ppo$kb$, $kb$difference$kb$, $kb$referral$kb$, $kb$network$kb$, $kb$pcp$kb$, $kb$travel$kb$, $kb$premium$kb$]::text[], 'medicare_reference', false, true),
($kb$lib-ab-ma-3$kb$, $kb$ab-ma-3$kb$, $kb$Medicare Advantage Plan Types$kb$, $kb$Special Needs Plans (SNP) types$kb$, $kb$There are three SNP types: C-SNP (Chronic Condition) — for diabetes, heart failure, ESRD, COPD, etc.; I-SNP (Institutional) — for nursing home or long-term care residents; D-SNP (Dual-Eligible) — for those with both Medicare and Medicaid. SNPs tailor benefits, provider networks, and drug formularies to the specific population. Enrollment requires documentation of the qualifying condition or status.$kb$, ARRAY[$kb$snp$kb$, $kb$c-snp$kb$, $kb$i-snp$kb$, $kb$d-snp$kb$, $kb$chronic$kb$, $kb$institutional$kb$, $kb$dual$kb$, $kb$special needs$kb$]::text[], 'medicare_reference', false, true),
($kb$lib-ab-ma-4$kb$, $kb$ab-ma-4$kb$, $kb$Medicare Advantage Plan Types$kb$, $kb$MA-PD vs MA-only$kb$, $kb$MA-PD (Medicare Advantage Prescription Drug) plans bundle Part A, B, and D coverage into one plan — most common type. MA-only plans cover Part A and B but exclude drug coverage; members must enroll in a standalone Part D (PDP) separately. When comparing plans, verify whether drug coverage is included to avoid gaps. MA-PD plans have one combined premium and one ID card.$kb$, ARRAY[$kb$ma-pd$kb$, $kb$ma-only$kb$, $kb$prescription$kb$, $kb$part d$kb$, $kb$pdp$kb$, $kb$bundle$kb$, $kb$drug$kb$, $kb$coverage$kb$]::text[], 'medicare_reference', false, true),
($kb$lib-ab-car-1$kb$, $kb$ab-car-1$kb$, $kb$MA Plan Details by Carrier$kb$, $kb$UnitedHealthcare (UHC) Medicare Advantage$kb$, $kb$UHC offers HMO, PPO, and D-SNP plans nationwide. Known for the UHC Medicare Advantage portfolio with AARP branding. Key features: $0 primary care copays on many plans, nationwide PPO network, SilverSneakers fitness benefit, dental/vision/hearing allowances ($0–$2,500/yr depending on plan), OTC benefit cards, and transportation. UHC also offers the only fully integrated D-SNP in select markets. Commission: advance available, paid monthly.$kb$, ARRAY[$kb$unitedhealthcare$kb$, $kb$uhc$kb$, $kb$aarp$kb$, $kb$silversneakers$kb$, $kb$ppo$kb$, $kb$d-snp$kb$, $kb$otc$kb$, $kb$dental$kb$]::text[], 'medicare_reference', false, true),
($kb$lib-ab-car-2$kb$, $kb$ab-car-2$kb$, $kb$MA Plan Details by Carrier$kb$, $kb$Humana Medicare Advantage$kb$, $kb$Humana offers HMO, PPO, and SNP plans with strong presence in the South and Midwest. Key features: Go365 wellness program, Healthy Foods card (select plans), OTC allowances, dental/vision/hearing, SilverSneakers or FitOn, transportation (up to 24 one-way trips). Humana's Honor plan targets veterans. Commission: advance and as-earned options, fast appointment process (3–5 business days).$kb$, ARRAY[$kb$humana$kb$, $kb$go365$kb$, $kb$healthy foods$kb$, $kb$honor$kb$, $kb$veteran$kb$, $kb$otc$kb$, $kb$snp$kb$, $kb$appointment$kb$]::text[], 'medicare_reference', false, true),
($kb$lib-ab-car-3$kb$, $kb$ab-car-3$kb$, $kb$MA Plan Details by Carrier$kb$, $kb$Aetna (CVS Health) Medicare Advantage$kb$, $kb$Aetna offers HMO, PPO, and D-SNP plans. Key features: $0 PCP on most plans, Aetna Medicare Eagle for veterans, dental/vision/hearing allowances, OTC benefit, gym memberships (SilverSneakers or GymPac), and care management programs. Aetna's D-SNPs coordinate with state Medicaid in select states. Commission: advance available, competitive FMV rates. Appointment via Aetna broker portal.$kb$, ARRAY[$kb$aetna$kb$, $kb$cvs$kb$, $kb$eagle$kb$, $kb$veteran$kb$, $kb$silver sneakers$kb$, $kb$d-snp$kb$, $kb$otc$kb$, $kb$broker$kb$]::text[], 'medicare_reference', false, true),
($kb$lib-ab-car-4$kb$, $kb$ab-car-4$kb$, $kb$MA Plan Details by Carrier$kb$, $kb$Centene / WellCare Medicare Advantage$kb$, $kb$WellCare (a Centene company) offers HMO, PPO, and SNP plans, often with competitive premiums ($0 or low). Key features: Flex Card for dental/vision/hearing/transportation, OTC allowance, grocery benefit on select D-SNPs, and robust chronic condition management. WellCare focuses heavily on SNP and dual-eligible markets. Commission: advance available. Appointment via Centene broker portal.$kb$, ARRAY[$kb$wellcare$kb$, $kb$centene$kb$, $kb$flex card$kb$, $kb$grocery$kb$, $kb$d-snp$kb$, $kb$snp$kb$, $kb$otc$kb$, $kb$dual$kb$]::text[], 'medicare_reference', false, true),
($kb$lib-ab-car-5$kb$, $kb$ab-car-5$kb$, $kb$MA Plan Details by Carrier$kb$, $kb$Blue Cross Blue Shield (BCBS) Medicare Advantage$kb$, $kb$BCBS plans operate as independent local licensees (e.g., Anthem, HCSC, Florida Blue, Highmark) so plans, networks, and benefits vary by state/region. Key features: broad PPO networks (especially Anthem EPO/PPO), $0 PCP, dental/vision/hearing, fitness (SilverSneakers or RenActive), and OTC. Commission and appointment processes vary by licensee — confirm with the local BCBS Medicare broker team.$kb$, ARRAY[$kb$bcbs$kb$, $kb$blue cross$kb$, $kb$anthem$kb$, $kb$highmark$kb$, $kb$florida blue$kb$, $kb$epo$kb$, $kb$ppo$kb$, $kb$state$kb$]::text[], 'medicare_reference', false, true),
($kb$lib-ab-car-6$kb$, $kb$ab-car-6$kb$, $kb$MA Plan Details by Carrier$kb$, $kb$Cigna Medicare Advantage$kb$, $kb$Cigna offers HMO and PPO plans in select markets. Key features: $0 preventive dental, vision and hearing allowances, Cigna Healthy Today app, OTC benefit, gym membership, and care management. Cigna's Health Improvement Program targets chronic conditions. Commission: advance available, appointment via Cigna broker portal. Cigna has a smaller geographic footprint — verify county availability.$kb$, ARRAY[$kb$cigna$kb$, $kb$healthy today$kb$, $kb$otc$kb$, $kb$gym$kb$, $kb$ppo$kb$, $kb$hmo$kb$, $kb$county$kb$, $kb$broker$kb$]::text[], 'medicare_reference', false, true),
($kb$lib-ab-car-7$kb$, $kb$ab-car-7$kb$, $kb$MA Plan Details by Carrier$kb$, $kb$Kaiser Permanente Medicare Advantage$kb$, $kb$Kaiser operates HMO plans in limited regions (CA, CO, GA, HI, MD, OR, VA, WA, DC). Known for integrated care model — plan and provider are the same system. Key features: $0 PCP, integrated EHR, pharmacy on-site, dental/vision on select plans, fitness benefit. Kaiser consistently earns high Star Ratings (often 4.5–5). Limited geographic footprint — only available in Kaiser service areas. Commission: as-earned, advance limited. Appointment via Kaiser broker portal.$kb$, ARRAY[$kb$kaiser$kb$, $kb$permanente$kb$, $kb$hmo$kb$, $kb$integrated$kb$, $kb$star rating$kb$, $kb$5-star$kb$, $kb$california$kb$, $kb$colorado$kb$, $kb$georgia$kb$]::text[], 'medicare_reference', false, true),
($kb$lib-ab-car-8$kb$, $kb$ab-car-8$kb$, $kb$MA Plan Details by Carrier$kb$, $kb$Devoted Health Medicare Advantage$kb$, $kb$Devoted Health is a newer MA carrier focused on seniors, available in select markets (FL, TX, IL, OH, LA, MS, AL, GA, SC, NC, PA, NY, NJ, CT, MA). Key features: $0 premium plans common, $0 PCP, Devoted Medical (virtual primary care), dental/vision/hearing, OTC card, transportation, and SilverSneakers. Devoted offers D-SNP and C-SNP plans in some markets. Commission: advance available, fast appointment. Smaller network — verify providers carefully.$kb$, ARRAY[$kb$devoted$kb$, $kb$devoted health$kb$, $kb$virtual care$kb$, $kb$otc$kb$, $kb$d-snp$kb$, $kb$c-snp$kb$, $kb$florida$kb$, $kb$texas$kb$, $kb$new carrier$kb$]::text[], 'medicare_reference', false, true),
($kb$lib-ab-car-9$kb$, $kb$ab-car-9$kb$, $kb$MA Plan Details by Carrier$kb$, $kb$Clover Health Medicare Advantage$kb$, $kb$Clover Health is a tech-forward MA carrier available in select counties (NJ, PA, GA, TX, MS, SC, FL, IL, AL, TN, AR, OH). Key features: $0 premium plans, $0 PCP, Clover Assistant (AI clinical decision support for providers), dental/vision/hearing, OTC, transportation, and in-home visits. Clover focuses on HMO and PPO plans. Commission: advance available. Appointment via Clover broker portal. Verify county availability — Clover is rapidly expanding.$kb$, ARRAY[$kb$clover$kb$, $kb$clover health$kb$, $kb$ai$kb$, $kb$in-home$kb$, $kb$otc$kb$, $kb$transportation$kb$, $kb$ppo$kb$, $kb$hmo$kb$, $kb$new jersey$kb$]::text[], 'medicare_reference', false, true),
($kb$lib-ab-car-10$kb$, $kb$ab-car-10$kb$, $kb$MA Plan Details by Carrier$kb$, $kb$Molina Healthcare Medicare Advantage$kb$, $kb$Molina focuses on Medicaid and dual-eligible populations, offering D-SNP and C-SNP plans in CA, TX, FL, IL, MI, OH, WA, NM, UT, WI, ID, NV, SC, and Puerto Rico. Key features: $0 premium, $0 PCP, integrated Medicaid-Medicare coordination, dental/vision/hearing, OTC, transportation, and care management for chronic conditions. Molina is ideal for dual-eligible clients. Commission: as-earned. Appointment via Molina broker portal.$kb$, ARRAY[$kb$molina$kb$, $kb$d-snp$kb$, $kb$c-snp$kb$, $kb$dual$kb$, $kb$medicaid$kb$, $kb$integrated$kb$, $kb$otc$kb$, $kb$california$kb$, $kb$texas$kb$]::text[], 'medicare_reference', false, true),
($kb$lib-ab-car-11$kb$, $kb$ab-car-11$kb$, $kb$MA Plan Details by Carrier$kb$, $kb$Alignment Healthcare Medicare Advantage$kb$, $kb$Alignment Healthcare offers HMO and PPO plans in CA, FL, NC, SC, TX, NV, AZ, and IL. Key features: $0 premium plans, $0 PCP, Alignment's AVA (AI-powered care model), dental/vision/hearing, OTC, transportation, and chronic care programs. Alignment focuses on seniors with complex needs and offers C-SNP plans. Commission: advance available. Appointment via Alignment broker portal.$kb$, ARRAY[$kb$alignment$kb$, $kb$alignment healthcare$kb$, $kb$ava$kb$, $kb$ai$kb$, $kb$c-snp$kb$, $kb$chronic$kb$, $kb$otc$kb$, $kb$california$kb$, $kb$florida$kb$]::text[], 'medicare_reference', false, true),
($kb$lib-ab-car-12$kb$, $kb$ab-car-12$kb$, $kb$MA Plan Details by Carrier$kb$, $kb$SCAN Health Plan Medicare Advantage$kb$, $kb$SCAN Health Plan operates HMO and SNP plans primarily in CA, AZ, NV, TX, and CO. Strong focus on seniors and dual-eligibles. Key features: $0 PCP, dental/vision/hearing, OTC, transportation, fitness (SilverSneakers), and robust care management. SCAN offers D-SNP and I-SNP plans. Known for high Star Ratings and member satisfaction. Commission: advance available. Appointment via SCAN broker portal.$kb$, ARRAY[$kb$scan$kb$, $kb$scan health$kb$, $kb$d-snp$kb$, $kb$i-snp$kb$, $kb$silver sneakers$kb$, $kb$otc$kb$, $kb$california$kb$, $kb$arizona$kb$, $kb$star rating$kb$]::text[], 'medicare_reference', false, true),
($kb$lib-ab-car-13$kb$, $kb$ab-car-13$kb$, $kb$MA Plan Details by Carrier$kb$, $kb$Health Net Medicare Advantage$kb$, $kb$Health Net (a Centene company) offers HMO, PPO, and SNP plans in CA, AZ, OR, and WA. Key features: $0 premium plans common, $0 PCP, dental/vision/hearing, OTC, transportation, and fitness. Health Net focuses heavily on the California market with D-SNP and C-SNP options. Commission: advance available. Appointment via Health Net/Centene broker portal. WellCare and Health Net are both Centene — verify which brand operates in your county.$kb$, ARRAY[$kb$health net$kb$, $kb$centene$kb$, $kb$d-snp$kb$, $kb$c-snp$kb$, $kb$otc$kb$, $kb$california$kb$, $kb$arizona$kb$, $kb$oregon$kb$, $kb$washington$kb$]::text[], 'medicare_reference', false, true),
($kb$lib-ab-car-14$kb$, $kb$ab-car-14$kb$, $kb$MA Plan Details by Carrier$kb$, $kb$Oscar Medicare Advantage (Oscar Tech)$kb$, $kb$Oscar offers HMO and PPO plans in select markets (FL, TX, NY, CA, NJ, others). Known for tech-forward member experience via the Oscar app. Key features: $0 PCP on select plans, virtual care (Oscar Virtual Visit), dental/vision/hearing, OTC, and care navigation. Oscar's MA footprint is smaller than its ACA exchange presence — verify county availability. Commission: advance available. Appointment via Oscar broker portal.$kb$, ARRAY[$kb$oscar$kb$, $kb$oscar health$kb$, $kb$virtual visit$kb$, $kb$app$kb$, $kb$otc$kb$, $kb$florida$kb$, $kb$texas$kb$, $kb$tech$kb$, $kb$broker$kb$]::text[], 'medicare_reference', false, true),
($kb$lib-ab-car-15$kb$, $kb$ab-car-15$kb$, $kb$MA Plan Details by Carrier$kb$, $kb$Highmark Blue Cross Medicare Advantage$kb$, $kb$Highmark (a BCBS licensee) operates in PA, WV, DE, and parts of NY. Key features: broad PPO and HMO networks, $0 PCP, dental/vision/hearing, fitness (RenActive), OTC, and chronic care management. Highmark offers D-SNP plans in PA. Commission and appointment via Highmark broker portal — processes differ from other BCBS licensees. Verify with the local Highmark Medicare team.$kb$, ARRAY[$kb$highmark$kb$, $kb$bcbs$kb$, $kb$blue cross$kb$, $kb$pennsylvania$kb$, $kb$west virginia$kb$, $kb$renactive$kb$, $kb$d-snp$kb$, $kb$ppo$kb$]::text[], 'medicare_reference', false, true),
($kb$lib-ab-car-16$kb$, $kb$ab-car-16$kb$, $kb$MA Plan Details by Carrier$kb$, $kb$Anthem Blue Cross Medicare Advantage$kb$, $kb$Anthem (a BCBS licensee, now Elevance Health) operates in CA, CO, CT, GA, IN, KY, ME, MO, NV, NH, NY, OH, VA, WI, and others. Key features: EPO and PPO networks (EPO = no out-of-network except emergencies), $0 PCP, dental/vision/hearing, fitness (SilverSneakers or Active&Fit), OTC, and care management. Anthem offers D-SNP and C-SNP plans. Commission: advance available. Appointment via Anthem broker portal.$kb$, ARRAY[$kb$anthem$kb$, $kb$elevance$kb$, $kb$bcbs$kb$, $kb$epo$kb$, $kb$ppo$kb$, $kb$silver sneakers$kb$, $kb$d-snp$kb$, $kb$c-snp$kb$, $kb$california$kb$]::text[], 'medicare_reference', false, true),
($kb$lib-ab-car-17$kb$, $kb$ab-car-17$kb$, $kb$MA Plan Details by Carrier$kb$, $kb$Florida Blue Medicare Advantage$kb$, $kb$Florida Blue (a BCBS licensee) operates HMO and PPO plans statewide in Florida. Key features: broad PPO network, $0 PCP, dental/vision/hearing, fitness, OTC, and transportation. Florida Blue offers D-SNP plans in select counties. Strong network in rural Florida counties where other carriers may not operate. Commission: advance available. Appointment via Florida Blue broker portal.$kb$, ARRAY[$kb$florida blue$kb$, $kb$bcbs$kb$, $kb$florida$kb$, $kb$ppo$kb$, $kb$hmo$kb$, $kb$d-snp$kb$, $kb$rural$kb$, $kb$otc$kb$, $kb$transportation$kb$]::text[], 'medicare_reference', false, true),
($kb$lib-ab-car-18$kb$, $kb$ab-car-18$kb$, $kb$MA Plan Details by Carrier$kb$, $kb$Humana Honor Plan (Veterans)$kb$, $kb$Humana Honor is a specialized MA plan for veterans, available in select markets. Key features: $0 premium, $0 PCP, VA coordination, dental/vision/hearing, OTC, transportation, and fitness. Honor plans may include enhanced benefits for veterans such as hearing aids and preventive care. No VA enrollment required — veterans with Medicare Part A and B qualify. Commission: advance available. Verify Honor plan availability by county.$kb$, ARRAY[$kb$humana$kb$, $kb$honor$kb$, $kb$veteran$kb$, $kb$va$kb$, $kb$hearing aid$kb$, $kb$preventive$kb$, $kb$otc$kb$, $kb$transportation$kb$]::text[], 'medicare_reference', false, true),
($kb$lib-ab-car-19$kb$, $kb$ab-car-19$kb$, $kb$MA Plan Details by Carrier$kb$, $kb$UnitedHealthcare Dual Complete (D-SNP)$kb$, $kb$UHC Dual Complete is the flagship D-SNP product, available in most states. Key features: $0 premium, $0 PCP, coordinated Medicaid-Medicare benefits, dental/vision/hearing, OTC, transportation (up to 24 one-way trips), healthy food card (select plans), and care management. UHC Dual Complete is fully integrated in select states (NY, OH, TX, others). Requires Medicaid eligibility verification. Commission: advance available. Ideal for dual-eligible clients.$kb$, ARRAY[$kb$uhc$kb$, $kb$unitedhealthcare$kb$, $kb$dual complete$kb$, $kb$d-snp$kb$, $kb$dual$kb$, $kb$medicaid$kb$, $kb$food card$kb$, $kb$otc$kb$, $kb$integrated$kb$]::text[], 'medicare_reference', false, true),
($kb$lib-ab-car-20$kb$, $kb$ab-car-20$kb$, $kb$MA Plan Details by Carrier$kb$, $kb$Aetna Medicare Eagle (Veterans)$kb$, $kb$Aetna Medicare Eagle is designed for veterans, available in select markets. Key features: $0 premium, $0 PCP, VA care coordination, dental/vision/hearing, OTC, transportation, and fitness. Eagle plans may include enhanced hearing and vision benefits. Veterans with Part A and B qualify — no VA enrollment needed. Commission: advance available. Verify Eagle plan availability by county — not all markets have it.$kb$, ARRAY[$kb$aetna$kb$, $kb$eagle$kb$, $kb$veteran$kb$, $kb$va$kb$, $kb$hearing$kb$, $kb$vision$kb$, $kb$otc$kb$, $kb$transportation$kb$, $kb$fitness$kb$]::text[], 'medicare_reference', false, true),
($kb$lib-ab-car-21$kb$, $kb$ab-car-21$kb$, $kb$MA Plan Details by Carrier$kb$, $kb$WellCare Value Script (Part D)$kb$, $kb$WellCare Value Script is a standalone Part D (PDP) plan available nationwide. Key features: low premium, broad formulary, preferred generic tier, and coverage during the donut hole. Value Script is a good option for clients staying on Original Medicare who need drug coverage. Full LIS beneficiaries may pay $0 on the benchmark version. Commission: ~$103 initial / $51 renewal. Appointment not required for PDP-only sales in most states.$kb$, ARRAY[$kb$wellcare$kb$, $kb$value script$kb$, $kb$part d$kb$, $kb$pdp$kb$, $kb$standalone$kb$, $kb$drug$kb$, $kb$formulary$kb$, $kb$lis$kb$, $kb$benchmark$kb$]::text[], 'medicare_reference', false, true),
($kb$lib-ab-car-22$kb$, $kb$ab-car-22$kb$, $kb$MA Plan Details by Carrier$kb$, $kb$SilverScript (CVS/Aetna) Part D$kb$, $kb$SilverScript is Aetna/CVS's standalone Part D plan, available nationwide. Key features: low premium, broad formulary, preferred pharmacy network (CVS), and donut hole coverage. SilverScript is one of the most-enrolled PDP plans. Full LIS beneficiaries may qualify for $0 premium. Commission: ~$103 initial / $51 renewal. No appointment needed for PDP-only enrollment.$kb$, ARRAY[$kb$silverscript$kb$, $kb$aetna$kb$, $kb$cvs$kb$, $kb$part d$kb$, $kb$pdp$kb$, $kb$drug$kb$, $kb$formulary$kb$, $kb$cvs pharmacy$kb$, $kb$lis$kb$]::text[], 'medicare_reference', false, true),
($kb$lib-ab-car-23$kb$, $kb$ab-car-23$kb$, $kb$MA Plan Details by Carrier$kb$, $kb$Mutual of Omaha Medicare Supplement (Medigap)$kb$, $kb$Mutual of Omaha is a top Medigap carrier. Key features: Plans A, B, C, D, F, G, High-Deductible G, K, L, M, and N available (Plan F only for those eligible before 2020). Plan G is the most popular — covers everything except Part B deductible. Medigap is guaranteed renewable and portable across all 50 states. Underwriting required in most states (not during IEP/OEP). Commission: 20–25% of premium for 6–9 years depending on plan. Appointment via Mutual of Omaha broker portal.$kb$, ARRAY[$kb$mutual of omaha$kb$, $kb$medigap$kb$, $kb$supplement$kb$, $kb$plan g$kb$, $kb$plan f$kb$, $kb$plan n$kb$, $kb$underwriting$kb$, $kb$portable$kb$, $kb$guaranteed renewable$kb$]::text[], 'medicare_reference', false, true),
($kb$lib-ab-car-24$kb$, $kb$ab-car-24$kb$, $kb$MA Plan Details by Carrier$kb$, $kb$AARP / UHC Medicare Supplement (Medigap)$kb$, $kb$UnitedHealthcare offers Medigap plans under the AARP branding. Key features: Plans A, B, C, F, G, High-Deductible G, K, L, and N. AARP/UHC Medigap is one of the most recognized and widely held. Plan G is the most popular (covers all but Part B deductible). Household discount available in most states. Commission: 20–25% of premium. Appointment via UHC broker portal. Underwriting required outside IEP/OEP.$kb$, ARRAY[$kb$aarp$kb$, $kb$uhc$kb$, $kb$unitedhealthcare$kb$, $kb$medigap$kb$, $kb$supplement$kb$, $kb$plan g$kb$, $kb$plan f$kb$, $kb$plan n$kb$, $kb$household discount$kb$]::text[], 'medicare_reference', false, true),
($kb$lib-ab-car-25$kb$, $kb$ab-car-25$kb$, $kb$MA Plan Details by Carrier$kb$, $kb$Blue Cross Blue Shield Medicare Supplement (Medigap)$kb$, $kb$BCBS licensees offer Medigap plans in their respective states. Key features: Plans A, B, C, D, F, G, High-Deductible G, K, L, M, and N (availability varies by state licensee). BCBS Medigap is popular due to brand recognition and broad acceptance. Household discounts available in many states. Commission: 20–25% of premium. Underwriting required outside IEP/OEP. Appointment processes vary by licensee.$kb$, ARRAY[$kb$bcbs$kb$, $kb$blue cross$kb$, $kb$medigap$kb$, $kb$supplement$kb$, $kb$plan g$kb$, $kb$plan n$kb$, $kb$household discount$kb$, $kb$underwriting$kb$, $kb$state$kb$]::text[], 'medicare_reference', false, true),
($kb$lib-ab-car-26$kb$, $kb$ab-car-26$kb$, $kb$MA Plan Details by Carrier$kb$, $kb$WellCare Medicare Supplement (Medigap)$kb$, $kb$WellCare offers Medigap plans in select states. Key features: Plans A, F, G, High-Deductible G, and N (availability varies). WellCare Medigap competes on price — premiums may be lower than Mutual of Omaha or AARP/UHC for the same plan letter. Commission: 20–25% of premium. Appointment via WellCare/Centene broker portal. Underwriting required outside IEP/OEP. Verify state availability.$kb$, ARRAY[$kb$wellcare$kb$, $kb$medigap$kb$, $kb$supplement$kb$, $kb$plan g$kb$, $kb$plan n$kb$, $kb$plan f$kb$, $kb$price$kb$, $kb$underwriting$kb$, $kb$centene$kb$]::text[], 'medicare_reference', false, true),
($kb$lib-ab-car-27$kb$, $kb$ab-car-27$kb$, $kb$MA Plan Details by Carrier$kb$, $kb$Humana Medicare Supplement (Medigap)$kb$, $kb$Humana offers Medigap plans in select states. Key features: Plans A, C, F, G, High-Deductible G, and N. Humana Medigap may include household discounts and online application in some states. Commission: 20–25% of premium. Appointment via Humana broker portal. Underwriting required outside IEP/OEP. Humana Medigap is a good cross-sell for clients who prefer Original Medicare over MA.$kb$, ARRAY[$kb$humana$kb$, $kb$medigap$kb$, $kb$supplement$kb$, $kb$plan g$kb$, $kb$plan n$kb$, $kb$plan f$kb$, $kb$household discount$kb$, $kb$underwriting$kb$, $kb$original medicare$kb$]::text[], 'medicare_reference', false, true),
($kb$lib-ab-car-28$kb$, $kb$ab-car-28$kb$, $kb$MA Plan Details by Carrier$kb$, $kb$Cigna Medicare Supplement (Medigap)$kb$, $kb$Cigna offers Medigap plans in select states. Key features: Plans A, B, C, D, F, G, High-Deductible G, K, L, and N. Cigna Medigap includes household discounts in many states and online application. Commission: 20–25% of premium. Appointment via Cigna broker portal. Underwriting required outside IEP/OEP. Cigna Medigap availability varies — check state.$kb$, ARRAY[$kb$cigna$kb$, $kb$medigap$kb$, $kb$supplement$kb$, $kb$plan g$kb$, $kb$plan n$kb$, $kb$plan f$kb$, $kb$household discount$kb$, $kb$underwriting$kb$, $kb$online$kb$]::text[], 'medicare_reference', false, true),
($kb$lib-ab-car-29$kb$, $kb$ab-car-29$kb$, $kb$MA Plan Details by Carrier$kb$, $kb$Carrier comparison: MA vs Medigap decision guide$kb$, $kb$When helping a client choose between Medicare Advantage and Medigap + Original Medicare: MA pros — lower or $0 premium, extra benefits (dental, vision, hearing, OTC, fitness), max out-of-pocket cap. MA cons — network restrictions, referrals (HMO), prior authorization, annual plan changes. Medigap pros — any Medicare provider nationwide, no referrals, predictable costs, portable. Medigap cons — higher monthly premium, no extra benefits, no drug coverage (need standalone PDP). For clients who travel, see specialists frequently, or want freedom, Medigap + PDP is often better. For budget-conscious clients who use in-network providers, MA is often better.$kb$, ARRAY[$kb$comparison$kb$, $kb$medigap$kb$, $kb$advantage$kb$, $kb$ma vs medigap$kb$, $kb$original medicare$kb$, $kb$network$kb$, $kb$premium$kb$, $kb$out of pocket$kb$, $kb$travel$kb$]::text[], 'medicare_reference', false, true),
($kb$lib-ab-car-30$kb$, $kb$ab-car-30$kb$, $kb$MA Plan Details by Carrier$kb$, $kb$Carrier appointment & contracting quick reference$kb$, $kb$Appointment process by carrier (approximate): UHC — online via UHC broker portal, 3–5 business days; Humana — online via Humana broker portal, 2–4 business days; Aetna — online via Aetna broker portal, 3–7 business days; WellCare/Centene — online via Centene broker portal, 5–10 business days; BCBS — varies by licensee, contact local Medicare broker team; Cigna — online via Cigna broker portal, 3–5 business days; Kaiser — restricted, contact Kaiser broker relations; Devoted/Clover/Alignment — online via respective portals, 3–7 business days. AHIP certification required annually before appointment with most carriers.$kb$, ARRAY[$kb$appointment$kb$, $kb$contracting$kb$, $kb$broker$kb$, $kb$portal$kb$, $kb$ahip$kb$, $kb$certification$kb$, $kb$carrier$kb$, $kb$process$kb$, $kb$timeline$kb$]::text[], 'medicare_reference', false, true),
($kb$lib-ab-car-31$kb$, $kb$ab-car-31$kb$, $kb$MA Plan Details by Carrier$kb$, $kb$Carrier Star Ratings overview (2025)$kb$, $kb$CMS Star Ratings (1–5) measure MA and Part D plan quality. 5-star plans allow year-round enrollment via 5-Star SEP. Recent high performers: Kaiser (4.5–5 in most markets), UHC (4–4.5 in many markets), Humana (4 in many markets), Devoted Health (4 in select markets). Ratings are updated each October. Lower-rated plans (2–3 stars) may face CMS penalties and reduced rebates. Always check current Star Ratings on CMS.gov before recommending — ratings change annually.$kb$, ARRAY[$kb$star rating$kb$, $kb$cms$kb$, $kb$5-star$kb$, $kb$quality$kb$, $kb$kaiser$kb$, $kb$uhc$kb$, $kb$humana$kb$, $kb$devoted$kb$, $kb$penalty$kb$, $kb$rating$kb$]::text[], 'medicare_reference', false, true),
($kb$lib-ab-car-32$kb$, $kb$ab-car-32$kb$, $kb$MA Plan Details by Carrier$kb$, $kb$OTC & supplemental benefit cards by carrier$kb$, $kb$OTC and supplemental benefit cards vary by carrier and plan: UHC — $0–$2,500/yr OTC + healthy food/produce card on select plans; Humana — Healthy Foods card + OTC on select plans (especially D-SNP); Aetna — OTC card + grocery on select D-SNPs; WellCare — Flex Card (dental/vision/hearing/transportation) + OTC + grocery on D-SNPs; Devoted — OTC + healthy food; Clover — OTC + transportation; Molina — OTC + transportation + healthy food on D-SNPs. Amounts and eligible items vary by plan — always verify in the plan's Evidence of Coverage (EOC).$kb$, ARRAY[$kb$otc$kb$, $kb$flex card$kb$, $kb$healthy food$kb$, $kb$grocery$kb$, $kb$produce$kb$, $kb$supplemental$kb$, $kb$benefit card$kb$, $kb$d-snp$kb$, $kb$carrier$kb$]::text[], 'medicare_reference', false, true),
($kb$lib-ab-ep-1$kb$, $kb$ab-ep-1$kb$, $kb$Election Periods$kb$, $kb$Annual Enrollment Period (AEP) — Oct 15 to Dec 7$kb$, $kb$The AEP (also called Open Enrollment) runs October 15 – December 7 each year. During AEP, beneficiaries can: join a Medicare Advantage plan, switch MA plans, switch from MA to Original Medicare + Part D, or switch Part D plans. Coverage changes take effect January 1. This is the busiest time for agents — all marketing and enrollment activity is concentrated here. SOA (Scope of Appointment) must be completed 48 hours before any in-home sales appointment during AEP.$kb$, ARRAY[$kb$aep$kb$, $kb$annual$kb$, $kb$open enrollment$kb$, $kb$october$kb$, $kb$december$kb$, $kb$january$kb$, $kb$soa$kb$, $kb$scope$kb$]::text[], 'medicare_reference', false, true),
($kb$lib-ab-ep-2$kb$, $kb$ab-ep-2$kb$, $kb$Election Periods$kb$, $kb$Medicare Advantage Open Enrollment Period (MA OEP) — Jan 1 to Mar 31$kb$, $kb$The MA OEP runs January 1 – March 31. Beneficiaries enrolled in an MA plan can make ONE change: switch to another MA plan, or disenroll from MA and return to Original Medicare (with or without a standalone Part D plan). Cannot switch Part D standalone plans during MA OEP (unless disenrolling from MA). Beneficiaries new to Medicare get a 3-month MA OEP starting the first month of Part B coverage. Marketing restrictions apply — agents cannot target MA OEP for marketing.$kb$, ARRAY[$kb$oep$kb$, $kb$ma oep$kb$, $kb$january$kb$, $kb$march$kb$, $kb$switch$kb$, $kb$disenroll$kb$, $kb$original medicare$kb$, $kb$one change$kb$]::text[], 'medicare_reference', false, true),
($kb$lib-ab-ep-3$kb$, $kb$ab-ep-3$kb$, $kb$Election Periods$kb$, $kb$Initial Enrollment Period (IEP)$kb$, $kb$The IEP is the 7-month window around a beneficiary's 65th birthday: 3 months before, the birthday month, and 3 months after. Beneficiaries can enroll in Medicare Part A, B, C (MA), and/or D. If enrolled during the first 3 months, coverage starts the birthday month. If enrolled during the birthday month or later months, coverage starts the following month. IEP also applies to those qualifying by disability (25-month SSDI).$kb$, ARRAY[$kb$iep$kb$, $kb$initial$kb$, $kb$65$kb$, $kb$birthday$kb$, $kb$7 month$kb$, $kb$part b$kb$, $kb$disability$kb$, $kb$ssdi$kb$]::text[], 'medicare_reference', false, true),
($kb$lib-ab-ep-4$kb$, $kb$ab-ep-4$kb$, $kb$Election Periods$kb$, $kb$Special Election Periods (SEP) overview$kb$, $kb$SEPs allow enrollment changes outside of AEP/MA OEP due to qualifying life events. Common SEPs: moving out of plan service area, losing employer coverage, losing Medicaid/LIS eligibility, entering/leaving a long-term care facility, CMS plan non-renewal, and 5-star SEP (enroll in a 5-star plan anytime, once per year). Each SEP has specific enrollment windows (typically 2–3 months after the triggering event). Documentation may be required.$kb$, ARRAY[$kb$sep$kb$, $kb$special election$kb$, $kb$move$kb$, $kb$employer$kb$, $kb$medicaid$kb$, $kb$lis$kb$, $kb$5-star$kb$, $kb$non-renewal$kb$, $kb$trigger$kb$]::text[], 'medicare_reference', false, true),
($kb$lib-ab-sep-1$kb$, $kb$ab-sep-1$kb$, $kb$Carrier SEP Requirements$kb$, $kb$SEP documentation requirements by carrier$kb$, $kb$Most carriers require SEP documentation before enrollment can be submitted. Common documents: proof of address change (utility bill, lease), loss of employer coverage (employer letter, COBRA notice), Medicaid/LIS status change (state notice), institutional admission/discharge (facility letter). UHC and Humana allow online SEP attestation for some SEPs but may request documentation post-enrollment. Aetna and WellCare typically require documentation upfront. Always verify with the carrier's enrollment guide.$kb$, ARRAY[$kb$sep$kb$, $kb$documentation$kb$, $kb$proof$kb$, $kb$address$kb$, $kb$employer$kb$, $kb$medicaid$kb$, $kb$attestation$kb$, $kb$carrier$kb$]::text[], 'medicare_reference', false, true),
($kb$lib-ab-sep-2$kb$, $kb$ab-sep-2$kb$, $kb$Carrier SEP Requirements$kb$, $kb$5-Star SEP — carrier availability$kb$, $kb$The 5-Star SEP allows enrollment into a CMS-rated 5-star MA or Part D plan at any time, once per year, without waiting for AEP. Not all carriers have 5-star plans in all markets — check CMS Star Ratings (published each October). As of recent ratings, select UHC, Humana, and Kaiser plans have held 5-star status in certain counties. The beneficiary must be enrolling in the specific 5-star-rated plan (not just any plan from a carrier with a 5-star plan elsewhere).$kb$, ARRAY[$kb$5-star$kb$, $kb$sep$kb$, $kb$star rating$kb$, $kb$cms$kb$, $kb$kaiser$kb$, $kb$uhc$kb$, $kb$humana$kb$, $kb$county$kb$]::text[], 'medicare_reference', false, true),
($kb$lib-ab-sep-3$kb$, $kb$ab-sep-3$kb$, $kb$Carrier SEP Requirements$kb$, $kb$Losing employer coverage SEP — carrier-specific notes$kb$, $kb$When a beneficiary loses employer/union group health coverage, they qualify for a SEP (2 months after loss of coverage). UHC: accepts employer attestation letter or COBRA notice; enrollment effective the month after submission. Humana: requires employer termination letter with date; fast-tracks within 48 hours. Aetna: accepts retirement or layoff documentation; may require Part B activation proof. WellCare: streamlined for loss of employer drug coverage (Part D SEP). Always confirm effective dates — they vary.$kb$, ARRAY[$kb$employer$kb$, $kb$loss$kb$, $kb$cobra$kb$, $kb$retirement$kb$, $kb$termination$kb$, $kb$part b$kb$, $kb$effective$kb$, $kb$carrier$kb$]::text[], 'medicare_reference', false, true),
($kb$lib-ab-sep-4$kb$, $kb$ab-sep-4$kb$, $kb$Carrier SEP Requirements$kb$, $kb$Moving SEP — service area change$kb$, $kb$When a beneficiary moves to a new address outside their current plan's service area, they qualify for a SEP (2 months before or 3 months after the move). If the new address has the same plan available, no change is required. If the plan is unavailable, the beneficiary must choose a new plan or return to Original Medicare. UHC and Humana accept new address via online attestation; Aetna and BCBS may require a utility bill or lease. D-SNP beneficiaries moving states must re-verify Medicaid status in the new state.$kb$, ARRAY[$kb$move$kb$, $kb$relocate$kb$, $kb$address$kb$, $kb$service area$kb$, $kb$new state$kb$, $kb$d-snp$kb$, $kb$medicaid$kb$, $kb$utility$kb$]::text[], 'medicare_reference', false, true),
($kb$lib-ab-na-1$kb$, $kb$ab-na-1$kb$, $kb$Needs Analysis & Fact Finding$kb$, $kb$Essential fact-finding questions for MA enrollment$kb$, $kb$Before recommending a Medicare Advantage plan, gather: 1) Current coverage (Original Medicare, MA, employer, Medicaid); 2) Doctors and specialists (names, NPIs, in-network verification); 3) Prescription drugs (name, dosage, frequency, pharmacy); 4) Monthly budget and premium tolerance; 5) Travel patterns (snowbirds, frequent travelers); 6) Chronic conditions and specialist needs; 7) Dental/vision/hearing needs; 8) Hospital or surgery anticipated in the next year. Document all answers on the needs assessment form.$kb$, ARRAY[$kb$fact finding$kb$, $kb$needs analysis$kb$, $kb$questions$kb$, $kb$doctors$kb$, $kb$drugs$kb$, $kb$budget$kb$, $kb$travel$kb$, $kb$chronic$kb$]::text[], 'medicare_reference', false, true),
($kb$lib-ab-na-2$kb$, $kb$ab-na-2$kb$, $kb$Needs Analysis & Fact Finding$kb$, $kb$Scope of Appointment (SOA) requirements$kb$, $kb$A Scope of Appointment (SOA) form must be completed at least 48 hours before any in-person or telephonic sales appointment for MA or Part D. The SOA documents which products will be discussed (MA, Part D, Medigap, etc.). Agents may only discuss and sell products listed on the SOA. SOA is not required for existing clients for service-related meetings or for Medigap-only discussions. Keep SOA on file for 10 years. CMS audits SOA compliance regularly.$kb$, ARRAY[$kb$soa$kb$, $kb$scope of appointment$kb$, $kb$48 hours$kb$, $kb$sales$kb$, $kb$cms$kb$, $kb$audit$kb$, $kb$document$kb$, $kb$compliance$kb$]::text[], 'medicare_reference', false, true),
($kb$lib-ab-na-3$kb$, $kb$ab-na-3$kb$, $kb$Needs Analysis & Fact Finding$kb$, $kb$Drug formulary verification process$kb$, $kb$Always verify the client's medications against each plan's formulary before recommending. Steps: 1) Collect complete drug list with dosages and frequencies; 2) Check each plan's formulary via carrier portal or Medicare Plan Finder; 3) Note tier levels (Tier 1 preferred generic to Tier 5 specialty); 4) Check for prior authorization, step therapy, or quantity limits; 5) Calculate total annual drug cost across plans. A plan with a $0 premium but Tier 4 for the client's main medication may cost more overall than a higher-premium plan.$kb$, ARRAY[$kb$formulary$kb$, $kb$drug$kb$, $kb$tier$kb$, $kb$prior auth$kb$, $kb$step therapy$kb$, $kb$plan finder$kb$, $kb$medication$kb$, $kb$cost$kb$]::text[], 'medicare_reference', false, true),
($kb$lib-ab-na-4$kb$, $kb$ab-na-4$kb$, $kb$Needs Analysis & Fact Finding$kb$, $kb$Provider network verification$kb$, $kb$Before recommending a plan, verify all the client's providers are in-network: 1) Collect provider names and NPIs; 2) Check each carrier's online provider directory or call provider relations; 3) Confirm primary care, specialists, hospitals, and ancillary (physical therapy, dialysis); 4) Note if any providers are out-of-network and assess impact (HMO = no coverage, PPO = higher cost). Document verification dates — directories change frequently. If a key provider is leaving the network, flag for the client.$kb$, ARRAY[$kb$provider$kb$, $kb$network$kb$, $kb$npi$kb$, $kb$directory$kb$, $kb$specialist$kb$, $kb$hospital$kb$, $kb$in-network$kb$, $kb$verify$kb$]::text[], 'medicare_reference', false, true),
($kb$lib-ab-na-5$kb$, $kb$ab-na-5$kb$, $kb$Needs Analysis & Fact Finding$kb$, $kb$Documenting the enrollment — required forms checklist$kb$, $kb$Required documents for a clean MA enrollment submission: 1) Signed SOA (48 hrs prior); 2) Completed needs assessment; 3) Plan enrollment application (paper or e-app); 4) SEP documentation (if applicable); 5) Proof of Part B activation (for IEP/SEP enrollments); 6) Medicaid/LIS documentation (for D-SNP); 7) Authorization for representative (if spouse/family assisting). Missing any item delays the enrollment. Submit via carrier portal and retain copies for 10 years per CMS retention rules.$kb$, ARRAY[$kb$document$kb$, $kb$enrollment$kb$, $kb$soa$kb$, $kb$application$kb$, $kb$sep$kb$, $kb$part b$kb$, $kb$d-snp$kb$, $kb$retention$kb$, $kb$cms$kb$]::text[], 'medicare_reference', false, true)
